  FT["MY-H3750"] = {"id":"MY-H3750","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 282/2023&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"1957年彩票（账簿）条例","en":"LOTTERIES (BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS) REGULATIONS 1957","orig":"LOTTERIES (BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS) REGULATIONS 1957","vi":"Quy định về Xổ số (Sổ sách kế toán) năm 1957","th":"ข้อบังคับสลากกินแบ่ง (สมุดบัญชี) ค.ศ. 1957","id":"Peraturan Lotere (Buku Akun) Tahun 1957","ms":"Peraturan Loteri (Buku Akaun) 1957"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA282","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2023","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 3 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2023_P.U.(A)282-2023_LOTTERIES (BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS) REGULATIONS 1957.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3750-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"1. Citation"}},{"id":"MY-H3750-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"2. Books of accounts"}},{"id":"MY-H3750-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"3. Forms\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nLAWS OF MALAYSIA\n\nLOTTERIES ACT 1952\n\n[ACT 288]\n\nLOTTERIES (BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS) REGULATIONS 1957\n\n(Made under section 14)\n\n(Revised—2023)\n\n[9 January 1958]\n\nCitation\n\n1. These regulations may be cited as the Lotteries (Books of Accounts)\n\nRegulations 1957.\n\nBooks of accounts\n\n2. The promoter of any lottery in respect of which a permit under section 4\n\nof the Act has been granted shall keep the following books of accounts:\n\n(a) a cash book; and\n\n(b) a register of tickets issued, sold and returned.\n\nForms\n\n3. The cash book and the register of tickets issued, sold and returned required to be\n\nkept under regulation 2 shall be in Forms A and B of the Schedule respectively.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n[Regulation 3]\n\nFORM A\n\nLOTTERIES (BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS) REGULATIONS 1957\n\nCASH BOOK\n\nRECEIPTS PAYMENTS\n\nDate Details Register of\n\ntickets\n\nissued\n\nreference\n\nCash Bank Date Details Cash Bank\n\nFORM B\n\nLOTTERIES (BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS) REGULATIONS 1957\n\nREGISTER OF TICKETS ISSUED, SOLD AND RETURNED\n\nISSUANCE OF TICKETS SALES OF TICKETS RETURN OF UNSOLD TICKETS\n\nDistinguishing\n\nnumber of\n\ntickets\n\ndistributed\n\nValue of\n\ntickets\n\ndistributed\n\nName of\n\nSeller or\n\nAgent\n\nDate of\n\ntickets\n\ndispatched\n\nTotal\n\nnumber of\n\ntickets\n\nsold\n\nGross\n\nvalue of\n\ntickets\n\nsold\n\nAmount of\n\nseller's\n\ncommission\n\nallowed\n\nReceipts Cash book\n\ncross\n\nreference\n\nNumbers\n\nof unsold\n\ntickets\n\nreturned\n\nValue of\n\nunsold\n\ntickets\n\nreturned\n\nDate of\n\nunsold\n\ntickets\n\nreturned\n\nLAWS OF MALAYSIA\n\nLOTTERIES ACT 1952\n\n[ACT 288]\n\nLOTTERIES (BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS) REGULATIONS 1957\n\n(Made under section 14)\n\n(Revised—2023)\n\nParticulars under paragraphs 7(ii) and (iii)\n\nof the Revision of Laws Act 1968 [Act 1]\n\nLIST OF AMENDMENTS\n\nAmending law Citation In force from\n\n-NIL-\n\n_____________________\n\nLIST OF LAWS OR PARTS THEREOF SUPERSEDED\n\nNo. Title\n\nL.N. 7/1958 Lotteries (Books of Accounts) Regulations, 1957\n\n_____________________"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3751"] = {"id":"MY-H3751","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 282/2024&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2024年大学与大学学院（沙巴大学章程）（修正）令","en":"UNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES (CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI MALAYSIA SABAH) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2024","orig":"UNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES (CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI MALAYSIA SABAH) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2024","ms":"Perintah Universiti dan Kolej Universiti (Perlembagaan Universiti Malaysia Sabah) (Pindaan) 2024","vi":"Lệnh về Các trường đại học và cao đẳng đại học (Quy chế Đại học Malaysia Sabah) (Sửa đổi) năm 2024","th":"คำสั่งมหาวิทยาลัยและวิทยาลัยมหาวิทยาลัย (ข้อกำหนดมหาวิทยาลัยมาเลเซียซาบาห์) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2024","id":"Perintah Universitas dan Kolese Universitas (Anggaran Dasar Universitas Malaysia Sabah) (Perubahan) Tahun 2024"},"level":"regulation","category":"01_宪法与基础法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA282","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2024","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\01_宪法与基础法\\2024_P.U.(A)282-2024_UNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES (CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI MALAYSIA SABAH) (AMENDMENT.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3751-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Universiti dan\nKolej Universiti (Perlembagaan Universiti Malaysia Sabah) (Pindaan) 2024.\n\n (2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 2 Oktober 2024.\n\nPindaan seksyen 57"}},{"id":"MY-H3751-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perlembagaan Universiti Malaysia Sabah  [P.U. (A) 460/2010 ] dipinda\ndalam seksyen 57—\n\n(a) dalam subseksyen (5), dengan menggantikan perkataan \"satu tahun\"\ndengan perkataan \"satu tahun akademik\";\n\n(b) dengan memasukkan selepas subseksyen (5) subseksyen yang berikut:\n\n\"(5A) Walau apa pun subseksyen (5), Lembaga boleh\nmengurangkan atau melanjutkan tempoh keahlian MPP dan\npemegang jawatannya.\";\n\n(c) dengan memotong subseksyen (11);\n\n(d) dengan memasukkan selepas subseksyen (11) sebagaimana yang dipotong\nsubseksyen yang berikut:\n\n\"(11A)      Universiti boleh menubuhkan apa -apa kumpulan wang\natau memiliki apa-apa harta untuk diuruskan atau disenggara oleh MPP\nmengikut tatacara kewangan Universiti.\n\n(11B)   Walau apa pun subseksyen  (11A), MPP boleh, tertakluk\nkepada mana -mana undang -undang bertulis, menubuhkan,\nmenguruskan atau menyenggara apa -apa kumpulan wang mengikut\ncara sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam peraturan -peraturan yang\ndibuat oleh Lembaga.\"; dan\n\n(e) dengan memasukkan selepas subseksyen (12) subseksyen yang berikut:\n\n\"(12A)   Bagi maksud seksyen 15 A Akta, Lembaga boleh membuat\nperaturan-peraturan untuk menetapkan cara bagi pembuatan atau\npenganjuran atau pengambilan bahagian dalam pungutan wang atau\npenerimaan wang atau sumbangan lain oleh MPP.\".\n\nDibuat  1 Oktober 2024\n[KPT.PUU(S).100-1/21/1(11); PN(PU2)75H/III]\n\nDengan Titah Perintah\n\nDATO' SERI DIRAJA DR. ZAMBRY BIN ABD KADIR\nMenteri Pendidikan Tinggi\n\nUNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES ACT 1971\n\nUNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES\n(CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI MALAYSIA SABAH) (AMENDMENT)\nORDER 2024\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 8(3) of the\nUniversities and University Colleges Act 1971 [Act 30], the Yang di-Pertuan Agong makes\nthe following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3752"] = {"id":"MY-H3752","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 282/2025&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2025年联邦道路（私营管理）（通行费征收）（蕉赖—加影大道）（修正）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (CHERAS-KAJANG HIGHWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (CHERAS-KAJANG HIGHWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Pengurusan Swasta) (Kutipan Tol) (Lebuh Raya Cheras-Kajang) (Pindaan) 2025","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Quản lý tư nhân) (Thu phí đường bộ) (Đường cao tốc Cheras-Kajang) (Sửa đổi) năm 2025","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (การบริหารจัดการเอกชน) (การจัดเก็บค่าผ่านทาง) (ทางหลวงเชอรัส-กาจัง) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2025","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Pengelolaan Swasta) (Pemungutan Tol) (Jalan Raya Cheras-Kajang) (Perubahan) Tahun 2025"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA282","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2025","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2025_P.U.(A)282-2025_FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (CHERAS-KAJANG HIGHWAY) (AMENDMENT) OR.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3752-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan\n\n(Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol) (Lebuhraya Cheras-Kajang)\n\n(Pindaan) 2025.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 31 Ogos 2025.\n\nPindaan Jadual Ketiga"}},{"id":"MY-H3752-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan (Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol)\n\n(Lebuhraya Cheras-Kajang) 1999 [P.U. (A) 15/1999] dipinda dalam Jadual Ketiga\n\ndengan memasukkan selepas butiran 6 butiran yang berikut:\n\n\"7. Mana-mana kenderaan Kerajaan yang mempunyai lambang rasmi\n\nJabatan Pengangkutan Jalan yang dilekatkan pada bahagian kiri dan kanan\n\nbadan kenderaan itu, dan dilekatkan secara kekal dengan lampu amaran\n\nkhas yang memancarkan cahaya berkelip biru pada bumbung kenderaan\n\nitu, bagi maksud menjalankan tugas penguatkuasaan.\".\n\nDibuat 26 Ogos 2025\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/43; PN(PU2)426/JLD.73]\n\nDATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\nMenteri Kerja Raya\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) ACT 1984\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS)\n\n(CHERAS-KAJANG HIGHWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of the Federal Roads\n\n(Private Management) Act 1984 [Act 306], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3753"] = {"id":"MY-H3753","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 282/2026&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2026年娱乐税（豁免）（第27号）令","en":"ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 27) ORDER 2026","orig":"ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 27) ORDER 2026","ms":"Perintah Duti Hiburan (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 27) 2026","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế giải trí (Miễn trừ) (số 27) năm 2026","th":"คำสั่งภาษีบันเทิง (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 27) ค.ศ. 2026","id":"Perintah Bea Hiburan (Pembebasan) (Nomor 27) Tahun 2026"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA282","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2026_P.U.(A)282-2026_ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 27) ORDER 2026.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3753-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Duti Hiburan (Pengecualian)\n\n(No. 27) 2026.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H3753-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Menteri mengecualikan tiket masuk bagi persembahan IVE WORLD TOUR SHOW\n\nWHAT I AM yang telah diadakan di Unifi Arena Bukit Jalil, Kuala Lumpur\n\npada 4 April 2026 daripada duti hiburan.\n\nDibuat 10 Julai 2026\n\n[MOF.700-4/6/33 JLD.2; PN(PU2)174/JLD.15]\n\nDATUK SERI AMIR HAMZAH BIN AZIZAN\n\n Menteri Kewangan II\n\nENTERTAINMENTS DUTY ACT 1953\n\nENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 27) ORDER 2026\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 12(1)(b)\n\nof the Entertainments Duty Act 1953 [Act 103], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3754"] = {"id":"MY-H3754","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2011&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2011年关税（计价）（棕榈油）（第34号）令","en":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 34) ORDER 2011","orig":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 34) ORDER 2011","ms":"Perintah Kastam (Nilai) (Minyak Sawit) (Bilangan 34) 2011","vi":"Lệnh về Hải quan (Trị giá) (Dầu cọ) (số 34) năm 2011","th":"คำสั่งศุลกากร (มูลค่า) (น้ำมันปาล์ม) (ฉบับที่ 34) ค.ศ. 2011","id":"Perintah Kepabeanan (Nilai) (Minyak Kelapa Sawit) (Nomor 34) Tahun 2011"},"level":"regulation","category":"03_涉外投资与贸易","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2011","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\03_涉外投资与贸易\\2011_P.U.(A)283-2011_CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 34) ORDER 2011.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3754-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kastam (Nilai -Nilai)\n(Minyak Kelapa Sawit) (No. 34) 2011 dan hendaklah mula berkuat kuasa bagi tempoh\ndari 22 Ogos 2011 hingga 28 Ogos 2011.\n\nPemungutan dan pembayaran duti kastam"}},{"id":"MY-H3754-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Bagi maksud pemungutan dan pembayaran duti -duti kastam, menurut\nperuntukan-peruntukan Perintah Duti Kastam 2007 [ P.U. (A) 441/2007], nilai bagi tiap -\ntiap satu barang berduti yang dinyatakan dalam ru ang (1) dan (2) Jadual mengikut\nunitnya yang tersebut dalam ruang (3) hendaklah nilai yang dinyatakan dalam\nruang (4).\n\nCUSTOMS ACT 1967\n\nCUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 34) ORDER 2011\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 12 of the Customs Act 1967 [Act 235], the\nMinister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\nJADUAL/SCHEDULE\nBarang\n(Goods)\n(1)\n\nSubkepala\n(Subheading)\n(2)\nUnit\n(Unit)\n(3)\nNilai\n(Value)\n(4)\nCrude Palm Oil 1511.10 100 tonne RM3,035.96\n\nDibuat  19 Ogos 2011\nMade  19 August 2011\n[KE.HT(94)819/03-6/KLT. 10(42); Perb.(8.20)116/1-4; PN(PU2)338/VIII]\n\nDengan arahan Menteri Kewangan/\nBy direction of the Minister of Finance\n\nBagi pihak dan atas nama Menteri Kewangan/\nOn behalf and in the name of the Minister of Finance\n\n DATO' SITI HALIMAH BINTI ISMAIL\n   Setiausaha/\nSecretary\nBahagian Analisa Cukai/\nTax Analysis Division"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3755"] = {"id":"MY-H3755","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2012&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2012年劳工（终止雇用与裁员福利）（沙巴）（修正）规则","en":"LABOUR (TERMINATION AND LAY-OFF BENEFITS) (SABAH) (AMENDMENT) RULES 2012","orig":"LABOUR (TERMINATION AND LAY-OFF BENEFITS) (SABAH) (AMENDMENT) RULES 2012","ms":"Kaedah Buruh (Faedah Penamatan dan Pemberhentian Kerja) (Sabah) (Pindaan) 2012","vi":"Quy tắc về Lao động (Phúc lợi chấm dứt hợp đồng và cho thôi việc) (Sabah) (Sửa đổi) năm 2012","th":"กฎแรงงาน (ผลประโยชน์การเลิกจ้างและการพักงาน) (ซาบาห์) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2012","id":"Tata Tertib Tenaga Kerja (Tunjangan Pemutusan Hubungan Kerja dan Perumahan Karyawan) (Sabah) (Perubahan) Tahun 2012"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2012","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2012_P.U.(A)283-2012_LABOUR (TERMINATION AND LAY-OFF BENEFITS) (SABAH) (AMENDMENT) RULES 2012.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3755-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Kaedah-kaedah ini bolehlah dinamakan Kaedah-Kaedah Buruh (Sabah)\n\n(Faedah Penamatan dan Pemberhentian Kerja Sementara) (Pindaan) 2012.\n\nPindaan kaedah 4"}},{"id":"MY-H3755-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Kaedah-Kaedah Buruh (Sabah) (Faedah Penamatan dan Pemberhentian Kerja\n\nSementara) 2008 [P.U. (A)159/2008] dipinda dalam subkaedah 4(1) —\n\n(a) dengan memasukkan selepas koma bernokhtah di hujung perenggan\n\n(b) perkataan \"atau\";\n\n(b) dengan menggantikan perkataan \"; atau\" di hujung perenggan (c)\n\ndengan nokhtah; dan\n\n(c) dengan memotong perenggan (d).\n\nDibuat 10 Ogos 2012\n\n[KSM/PUU/T/01/04 Jld.2; PN(PU2)207/IX]\n\n DATUK SERI DR. SUBRAMANIAM A/L K.V. SATHASIVAM\n\n Menteri Sumber Manusia\n\nLABOUR ORDINANCE OF SABAH\n\nLABOUR (TERMINATION AND LAY-OFF BENEFITS) (SABAH) (AMENDMENT) RULES\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 130o(2)(k) of the Labour Ordinance\n\nof Sabah [Sabah Cap. 67], the Minister after consultation with the State Authority, makes\n\nthe following rules:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3756"] = {"id":"MY-H3756","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2013&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2013年旅馆（吉隆坡联邦直辖区）（违法行为罚款了结）条例","en":"HOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES) REGULATIONS 2013","orig":"HOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES) REGULATIONS 2013","ms":"Peraturan Hotel (Wilayah Persekutuan Kuala Lumpur) (Pengkompaunan Kesalahan) 2013","vi":"Quy định về Khách sạn (Lãnh thổ Liên bang Kuala Lumpur) (Xử lý vi phạm bằng phạt tiền) năm 2013","th":"ข้อบังคับโรงแรม (เขตการปกครองสหพันธ์กัวลาลัมเปอร์) (การระงับข้อหาด้วยค่าปรับ) ค.ศ. 2013","id":"Peraturan Hotel (Wilayah Persekutuan Kuala Lumpur) (Penyelesaian Pelanggaran dengan Denda) Tahun 2013"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2013","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 6 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2013_P.U.(A)283-2013_HOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES) REGULATIONS 2013.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3756-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Nama dan permulaan kuat kuasa"}},{"id":"MY-H3756-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Kesalahan yang boleh dikompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H3756-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Tawaran dan penyetujuterimaan kompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H3756-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Cara mengkompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H3756-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Pembayaran kompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H3756-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"ms":"6. Pembatalan dan peruntukan peralihan\n\nJADUAL\n\nAKTA HOTEL (WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN KUALA LUMPUR) 2003\n\nPERATURAN-PERATURAN HOTEL (WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN KUALA LUMPUR)\n\n(PENGKOMPAUNAN KESALAHAN) 2013\n\nPADA menjalankan kuasa yang diberikan oleh perenggan 35(2)(d) Akta Hotel\n\n(Wilayah Persekutuan Kuala Lumpur) 2003 [Akta 626], Datuk Bandar, dengan kelulusan\n\nMenteri membuat peraturan-peraturan yang berikut:\n\nNama dan permulaan kuat kuasa\n\n1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\n\nHotel (Wilayah Persekutuan Kuala Lumpur) (Pengkompaunan Kesalahan) 2013.\n\n(2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 9 September 2013.\n\nKesalahan yang boleh dikompaun\n\n2. Kesalahan di bawah subseksyen 9(2) dan 12(4) Akta ditetapkan sebagai\n\nkesalahan yang boleh dikompaun.\n\nTawaran dan penyetujuterimaan kompaun\n\n3. (1) Suatu tawaran untuk mengkompaun suatu kesalahan hendaklah dibuat\n\ndalam Borang 1 Jadual.\n\n(2) Seseorang yang menyetuju terima tawaran untuk mengkompaun suatu\n\nkesalahan yang boleh dikompaun hendaklah mengemukakan bayaran bagi kompaun itu\n\ndalam Borang 2 Jadual.\n\n(3) Borang 1 dan 2 Jadual hendaklah digunakan bagi tujuan yang ditunjukkan\n\ndalam kandungannya tetapi tiada penyimpangan daripada Borang itu boleh\n\nmenidaksahkan atau menjejaskan kesahan apa-apa kandungan yang dibuat setakat\n\nyang penyimpangan itu tidak mempunyai kesan substansial dan tidak dikira\n\nmengelirukan.\n\nCara mengkompaun\n\n4. (1) Setelah suatu penyiasatan dijalankan dan didapati bahawa suatu\n\nkesalahan yang boleh dikompaun telah dilakukan, Datuk Bandar boleh, dengan\n\npersetujuan Pendakwa Raya, mengeluarkan suatu Notis Tawaran untuk Mengkompaun\n\nKesalahan dalam Borang 1 Jadual.\n\n(2) Tawaran untuk mengkompaun suatu kesalahan adalah bagi tempoh\n\nempat belas hari, dan jika pembayaran penuh bagi jumlah yang ditawarkan itu dibuat\n\npada atau sebelum habis tempoh empat belas hari itu, tiada prosiding selanjutnya boleh\n\ndiambil terhadap orang yang telah melakukan kesalahan itu.\n\n(3) Jika tiada pembayaran bagi kompaun yang telah ditawarkan itu dibuat\n\npada atau sebelum habis tempoh masa yang dinyatakan dalam subperaturan (2),\n\npendakwaan boleh dimulakan tanpa notis selanjutnya.\n\nPembayaran kompaun\n\n5. (1) Jika suatu tawaran untuk mengkompaun kesalahan dibuat dan disetuju\n\nterima oleh orang yang kepadanya tawaran itu dibuat, dia hendaklah membuat\n\npembayaran bagi kompaun—\n\n(a) secara tunai dan diserahkan sendiri;\n\n(b) melalui kiriman wang, kiriman wang pos, pesanan juruwang,\n\npesanan bank atau draf bank yang kena dibayar kepada Datuk\n\nBandar Kuala Lumpur dan dipalang dengan perkataan \"Akaun\n\nPenerima Sahaja\" dan boleh diserahkan sendiri atau dihantar\n\nmelalui pos kepada Datuk Bandar Kuala Lumpur, Peti Surat 11022,\n\nKuala Lumpur; atau\n\n(c) melalui kad kredit atau pemindahan wang secara elektronik yang\n\nlain.\n\n(2) Suatu resit rasmi hendaklah dikeluarkan bagi tiap-tiap pembayaran yang\n\nditerima di bawah subperaturan (1) kepada orang yang kepadanya tawaran untuk\n\nmengkompaun itu telah dibuat.\n\n(3) Suatu resit rasmi yang dikeluarkan bagi maksud subperaturan (2)\n\ntermasuk apa-apa resit elektronik yang dikeluarkan jika pembayaran dibuat melalui\n\nkad kredit atau pemindahan wang secara elektronik yang lain.\n\nPembatalan dan peruntukan peralihan\n\n6. (1) Peraturan-Peraturan Hotel (Wilayah Persekutuan Kuala Lumpur)\n\n(Pengkompaunan Kesalahan) 2005 [P.U. (A) 279/2005] dibatalkan.\n\n(2) Walau apa pun subperaturan (1), mana-mana notis yang dikeluarkan\n\ndi bawah Peraturan-Peraturan yang dibatalkan hendaklah terus sah seolah-olah ia\n\ndikeluarkan di bawah Peraturan-Peraturan ini.\n\nJADUAL\n\n[Peraturan 3 dan 4]\n\nBORANG 1\n\nAKTA HOTEL (WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN KUALA LUMPUR) 2003\n\nPERATURAN-PERATURAN HOTEL (WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN KUALA LUMPUR)\n\n(PENGKOMPAUNAN KESALAHAN) 2013\n\nNOTIS TAWARAN UNTUK MENGKOMPAUN KESALAHAN\n\nApabila menjawab sila nyatakan:\n\nNombor rujukan: ....................................................\n\nTarikh: .........................................................................\n\nKepada:\n\n.........................................................................................\n\n.........................................................................................\n\n.........................................................................................\n\nTuan/Puan*,\n\nSuatu penyiasatan telah dijalankan terhadap anda/...........................................................................\n\n…………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………*\n\n (nyatakan nama syarikat/perniagaan/badan lain*)\n\ndan anda didapati telah melakukan kesalahan yang berikut di bawah Akta Hotel\n\n(Wilayah Persekutuan Kuala Lumpur) 2003 [Akta 626] dengan butir-butir yang berikut:\n\n(a) Peruntukan yang berkenaan dalam Akta:\n\n……………………….........................................................................................................................\n\n.....................................……………………………....................................................................\n\n(b) Tarikh: ...............................................\n\n(c) Masa: ..................................................\n\n(d) Tempat: .............................................\n\n(e) Butir-butir kesalahan:\n\n.....................................................................................................................................................\n\n.....................................................................................................................................................\n\n.....................................................................................................................................................\n\n2. Menurut subseksyen 32(1) Akta, anda ditawarkan kompaun bagi kesalahan yang\n\ndinyatakan di atas bagi jumlah wang sebanyak RM..................................... (...................................\n\nringgit).\n\n3. Jika tawaran di atas diterima, pembayaran boleh dibuat—\n\n(a) secara tunai dan diserahkan sendiri;\n\n(b) melalui kiriman wang/kiriman wang pos/pesanan juruwang/pesanan\n\nbank/draf bank* yang kena dibayar kepada Datuk Bandar Kuala Lumpur\n\ndan dipalang dengan perkataan \"Akaun Penerima Sahaja\" dan boleh\n\ndiserahkan sendiri atau dihantar melalui pos kepada Datuk Bandar Kuala\n\nLumpur, Peti Surat 11022, Kuala Lumpur; atau\n\n(c) melalui kad kredit atau pemindahan wang secara elektronik yang lain.\n\n4. Suatu resit rasmi akan dikeluarkan apabila pembayaran kompaun itu diterima.\n\n5. Tawaran untuk mengkompaun ini akan bermula pada ...................................... dan\n\nberkuat kuasa sehingga ......................................, dan jika tiada pembayaran diterima pada\n\natau sebelum tarikh itu, pendakwaan bagi kesalahan akan dimulakan tanpa notis\n\nselanjutnya.\n\nTarikh : .................................\n\n.………….…......................................................................................\n\n Untuk dan bagi pihak Datuk Bandar Kuala Lumpur\n\nNama:\n\nJawatan:\n\nCop rasmi:\n\n* Potong mana-mana yang tidak berkenaan\n\nBORANG 2\n\n[Peraturan 3]\n\nAKTA HOTEL (WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN KUALA LUMPUR) 2003\n\nPERATURAN-PERATURAN HOTEL (WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN KUALA LUMPUR)\n\n(PENGKOMPAUNAN KESALAHAN) 2013\n\nPENYETUJUTERIMAAN TAWARAN UNTUK MENGKOMPAUN KESALAHAN\n\nKepada:\n\nDatuk Bandar Kuala Lumpur\n\nDewan Bandaraya Kuala Lumpur\n\nSaya merujuk kepada Notis Tawaran untuk Mengkompaun Kesalahan dengan nombor\n\nrujukan .......................................... dan bertarikh ...........................................\n\n2. Saya mengaku bahawa saya telah melakukan kesalahan ini dan saya bersetuju\n\nterima tawaran untuk mengkompaun itu dan disertakan bersama ini wang\n\ntunai/kiriman wang/kiriman wang pos/pesanan juruwang/pesanan bank/draf bank\n\nNo.* .............................. bagi jumlah wang sebanyak RM................................. ( ..............................\n\nringgit) sebagai penyelesaian penuh bagi jumlah wang yang dinyatakan dalam\n\nperenggan 2 Notis Tawaran untuk Mengkompaun Kesalahan.\n\nTandatangan: ........................................................\n\nNama (huruf besar): ...........................................\n\nNombor Kad Pengenalan: ................................\n\nJawatan: ...................................................................\n\nNama syarikat/perniagaan atau badan lain*: ..................................................................................\n\nMeterai syarikat/Cap perniagaan atau badan lain (jika berkenaan): ….................................\n\nNo. Pendaftaran Syarikat/No. Lesen/No. Permit (jika berkenaan): ........................................\n\nAlamat: .............................................................................................................................................................\n\n...............................................................................................................................................................................\n\nTarikh: ..........................................................................\n\n* Potong mana-mana yang tidak berkenaan\n\nDibuat 12 Julai 2013\n\n[JHEU2/97/2003; PN(PU2)642]\n\nDATUK SERI AHMAD PHESAL BIN TALIB\n\n Datuk Bandar Kuala Lumpur\n\nDiluluskan\n\n DATUK SERI UTAMA TENGKU ADNAN BIN TENGKU MANSOR\n\n Menteri Wilayah Persekutuan\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) ACT 2003\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\nREGULATIONS 2013\n\n__________________________________\n\nARRANGEMENT OF REGULATIONS\n\n__________________________________\n\nRegulations\n\n1. Citation and commencement\n\n2. Compoundable offences\n\n3. Offer and acceptance of compound\n\n4. Method of compounding\n\n5. Payment of compound\n\n6. Revocation and transitional provision\n\n SCHEDULE\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) ACT 2003\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\nREGULATIONS 2013\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 35(2)(d) of the Hotels\n\n(Federal Territory of Kuala Lumpur) Act 2003 [Act 626], the Commisioner, with the\n\napproval of the Minister makes the following regulations:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Hotels (Federal Territory of\n\nKuala Lumpur) (Compounding of Offences) Regulations 2013.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 9 September 2013.\n\nCompoundable offences\n\n2. The offences under subsections 9(2) and 12(4) of the Act are prescribed to be\n\ncompoundable offences.\n\nOffer and acceptance of compound\n\n3. (1) An offer to compound an offence shall be made in Form 1 of the Schedule.\n\n(2) A person who accepts an offer to compound a compoundable offence shall\n\nfurnish payment for the compound in Form 2 of the Schedule.\n\n(3) Forms 1 and 2 of the Schedule shall be used for the purpose indicated by\n\nits content but no deviation from the Form shall invalidate or affect the legality of any\n\ncomposition made so far as the deviation has no substantial effect and is not calculated\n\nto mislead.\n\nMethod of compounding\n\n4. (1) After an investigation has been conducted and it is found that a\n\ncompoundable offence has been committed, the Commissioner may, with the consent of\n\nthe Public Prosecutor, issue a Notice of Offer to Compound an Offence in Form 1 of the\n\nSchedule.\n\n(2) An offer to compound an offence is for a period of fourteen days, and if\n\nfull payment of the sum offered is made on or before the expiry of fourteen days, no\n\nfurther proceedings shall be taken against the person who committed such offence.\n\n(3) If no payment of the compound offered is made on or before the expiry of\n\nthe period stated in subregulation (2), prosecution may be instituted without further\n\nnotice.\n\nPayment of compound\n\n5. (1) If an offer to compound an offence is made and accepted by the person to\n\nwhom the offer is made, he shall make payment of the compound—\n\n(a) by cash and delivered personally;\n\n(b) by money order, postal order, cashier's order, banker's order or\n\nbank draft made payable to the Commissioner of the City of Kuala\n\nLumpur and crossed with the words \"Account Payee Only\" and\n\nmay be delivered personally or sent by post to the Commissioner\n\nof the City of Kuala Lumpur, P.O. Box 11022, Kuala Lumpur; or\n\n(c) by credit card or any other electronic fund transfers.\n\n(2) An official receipt shall be issued for every payment received under\n\nsubregulation (1) to the person to whom the offer to compound is made.\n\n(3) An official receipt issued for the purpose of subregulation (2) includes any\n\nelectronic receipt issued if the payment is made through credit card or other electronic\n\nfund transfers.\n\nRevocation and transitional provision\n\n6. (1) The Hotel (Federal Territory of Kuala Lumpur) (Compounding of\n\nOffences) Regulations 2005 [P.U. (A) 279/2005] are revoked.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding subregulation (1), any notice issued under the revoked\n\nRegulations shall continue to be valid as if it is issued under these Regulations.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n[Regulations 3 and 4]\n\nFORM 1\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) ACT 2003\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\nREGULATIONS 2013\n\nNOTICE OF OFFER TO COMPOUND AN OFFENCE\n\nWhen replying please quote:\n\nReference number: ...................................\n\nDate: ................................................................\n\nTo:\n\n............................................................................\n\n............................................................................\n\n............................................................................\n\nSir/Madam*,\n\nAn investigation has been conducted against you/..........................................................................\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………………………………….……*\n\n(state name of company/business/other body*)\n\nand you are found to have committed the following offence under the Hotels\n\n(Federal Territory of Kuala Lumpur) Act 2003 [Act 626] with the following particulars:\n\n(a) Relevant provision of the Act:\n\n……….........................................................................................................................................\n\n....................................................................................................................................................\n\n(b) Date: ................................................\n\n(c) Time: ...............................................\n\n(d) Place: ...............................................\n\n(e) Particulars of offence:\n\n..………………….………………………......................................................................................\n\n…………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n…………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n2. Pursuant to subsection 32(1) of the Act, you are offered a compound for the\n\noffence as stated above for the sum of RM…………..…………......… (…………………...………\n\nringgit).\n\n3. If the above offer to compound is accepted, payment may be made—\n\n(a) by cash and delivered personally;\n\n(b) by money order/postal order/cashier's order/banker's order/banker's\n\ndraft* made payable to the Commissioner of the City of Kuala Lumpur and\n\ncrossed with the words \"Account Payee Only\" and may be delivered\n\npersonally or sent by post to the Commissioner of the City of Kuala\n\nLumpur. P.O. Box 11022, Kuala Lumpur; or\n\n(c) by credit card or any other electronic fund transfers.\n\n4. An official receipt shall be issued on receipt of payment of the compound.\n\n5. This offer to compound will commence on ............................................... remains in\n\nforce until ……………………….........................., and if no payment is received on or before the\n\ndate, prosecution for the offence will be instituted without further notice.\n\nDate: .........................................\n\n ……………..................................................................................\n\n For and on behalf of the Commissioner of the\n\n City of Kuala Lumpur\n\nName:\n\nDesignation:\n\nOfficial stamp:\n\n* Delete whichever is inapplicable\n\nFORM 2\n\n[Regulation 3]\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) ACT 2003\n\nHOTELS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF KUALA LUMPUR) (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\nREGULATIONS 2013\n\nACCEPTANCE OF OFFER TO COMPOUND AN OFFENCE\n\nTo:\n\nThe Commissioner of the City of Kuala Lumpur\n\nCity Hall of Kuala Lumpur\n\nI refer to the Notice of Offer to Compound an Offence bearing the reference number\n\n……….................................. and dated .................................................\n\n2. I admit that I have committed the offence and I accept the offer to compound and\n\nenclose herewith cash/money order/postal order/cashier's order/banker's order/\n\nbanker's draft No.* ............................ for the sum of RM…......................................\n\n(……………........................... ringgit) as full settlement of the sum stipulated in paragraph 2 of\n\nthe Notice of Offer to Compound an Offence.\n\nSignature: ..........................................................................................\n\nName (in capital letter): ...............................................................\n\nIdentity Card Number: .................................................................\n\nDesignation: …..................................................................................\n\nName of company/business or other body*: …………………………………………….…………….\n\nCompany seal/Stamp of business or other body (if applicable):…………………………...........\n\nCompany Registration No. /Licence No./Permit No. (if applicable): ….……………………....\n\nAddress : …………………………........................................................................................................................\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………….\n\nDate: ................................................................................\n\n* Delete whichever is inapplicable\n\nMade 12 July 2013\n\n[JHEU2/97/2003; PN(PU2)642]\n\n DATUK SERI AHMAD PHESAL BIN TALIB\n\n Commissioner of the City of Kuala Lumpur\n\nApproved\n\n DATUK SERI UTAMA TENGKU ADNAN BIN TENGKU MANSOR\n\n Minister of Federal Territories"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3757"] = {"id":"MY-H3757","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2014&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2014年印刷机与出版物（不良出版物管制）（第10号）令","en":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2014","orig":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2014","ms":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Kawalan Penerbitan Tidak Diingini) (Bilangan 10) 2014","vi":"Lệnh về Máy in và ấn phẩm (Kiểm soát ấn phẩm không mong muốn) (số 10) năm 2014","th":"คำสั่งแท่นพิมพ์และสิ่งพิมพ์ (การควบคุมสิ่งพิมพ์ที่ไม่พึงประสงค์) (ฉบับที่ 10) ค.ศ. 2014","id":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Pengendalian Terbitan Tidak Diinginkan) (Nomor 10) Tahun 2014"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2014","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2014_P.U.(A)283-2014_PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2014.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3757-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan\n\n(Kawalan Hasil Penerbitan Tidak Diingini) (No. 10) 2014.\n\nLarangan"}},{"id":"MY-H3757-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Pencetakan, pengimportan, penghasilan, penghasilan semula, penerbitan,\n\npenjualan, pengeluaran, pengelilingan, pengedaran atau pemilikan hasil penerbitan\n\nyang diperihalkan dalam Jadual yang mungkin memudaratkan ketenteraman awam dan\n\nyang mungkin menggemparkan fikiran orang ramai adalah dilarang secara mutlak\n\ndi seluruh Malaysia.\n\nJADUAL\n\nTajuk Hasil\n\nPenerbitan\n\nPengarang/\n\nPenyusun\n\nPenerbit Pencetak Bahasa\n\nKisah Paling\n\nMenarik Yang\n\nPernah Diceritakan\n\n- Bibles\n\nInternational of\n\nCanada, #548-800,\n\n15355 24th Avenue,\n\nSurrey, BC Canada\n\nV4A 2H9\n\n- Indonesia\n\nDibuat 9 Oktober 2014\n\n[KDN:PQ(S) 600-2/1 Jld. 2-(10); PN(PU2)417/XII]\n\nDATO' SERI DR. AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\n\nMenteri Dalam Negeri\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS ACT 1984\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS\n\n(CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2014\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 7(1) of the Printing Presses and\n\nPublications Act 1984 [Act 301], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation\n\n1. This order may be cited as the Printing Presses and Publications\n\n(Control of Undesirable Publications) (No. 10) Order 2014.\n\nProhibition\n\n2. The printing, importation, production, reproduction, publishing, sale, issue,\n\ncirculation, distribution or possession of the publication described in the Schedule\n\nwhich is likely to be prejudicial to public order and likely to alarm public opinion, is\n\nabsolutely prohibited throughout Malaysia.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nTitle of\n\nPublication\n\nAuthor/\n\nCompiler\n\nPublisher Printer Language\n\nKisah Paling\n\nMenarik Yang\n\nPernah Diceritakan\n\n- Bibles\n\nInternational of\n\nCanada, #548-800,\n\n15355 24th Avenue,\n\nSurrey, BC Canada\n\nV4A 2H9\n\n- Indonesian\n\nMade 9 October 2014\n\n[KDN:PQ(S) 600-2/1 Jld. 2-(10); PN(PU2)417/XII]\n\nDATO' SERI DR. AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\n\nMinister of Home Affairs"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3758"] = {"id":"MY-H3758","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2015&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2015年护照（中华人民共和国旅客签证）（豁免）（修正）令","en":"PASSPORT (VISA TO TOURIST FROM THE PEOPLE’S REPUBLIC OF CHINA) (EXEMPTION) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2015","orig":"PASSPORT (VISA TO TOURIST FROM THE PEOPLE’S REPUBLIC OF CHINA) (EXEMPTION) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2015","ms":"Perintah Pasport (Visa kepada Pelancong dari Republik Rakyat China) (Pengecualian) (Pindaan) 2015","vi":"Lệnh về Hộ chiếu (Thị thực cho khách du lịch từ Cộng hòa Nhân dân Trung Hoa) (Miễn trừ) (Sửa đổi) năm 2015","th":"คำสั่งหนังสือเดินทาง (วีซ่าสำหรับนักท่องเที่ยวจากสาธารณรัฐประชาชนจีน) (การยกเว้น) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2015","id":"Perintah Paspor (Visa bagi Wisatawan dari Republik Rakyat Tiongkok) (Pembebasan) (Perubahan) Tahun 2015"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2015","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2015_P.U.(A)283-2015_PASSPORT (VISA TO TOURIST FROM THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA) (EXEMPTION) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 20.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3758-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Pasport\n\n(Visa kepada Pelancong daripada Republik Rakyat China) (Pengecualian)\n\n(Pindaan) 2015.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Disember 2015\n\nhingga 31 Mac 2016.\n\nPindaan perenggan 2"}},{"id":"MY-H3758-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Pasport (Visa kepada Pelancong daripada Republik Rakyat China)\n\n(Pengecualian) 2015 [P.U. (A) 221/2015] dipinda dalam subperenggan 2(b) dengan\n\nmenggantikan perkataan \"dua puluh\" dengan perkataan \"dua\".\n\nDibuat 30 November 2015\n\n[KDN(S):IM 03/208/4 Jld 2; PN(PU2)482]\n\nDATUK NUR JAZLAN BIN MOHAMED\n\nTimbalan Menteri Dalam Negeri I\n\nPASSPORT ACT 1966\n\nPASSPORT (VISA TO TOURIST FROM THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA)\n\n(EXEMPTION) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2015\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 4 of the Passport Act [Act 150],\n\nthe Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3759"] = {"id":"MY-H3759","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2016&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2016年消费税（浮罗交怡）令","en":"EXCISE DUTIES (LANGKAWI) ORDER 2016","orig":"EXCISE DUTIES (LANGKAWI) ORDER 2016","ms":"Perintah Duti Eksais (Langkawi) 2016","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế tiêu thụ đặc biệt (Langkawi) năm 2016","th":"คำสั่งภาษีสรรพสามิต (ลังกาวี) ค.ศ. 2016","id":"Perintah Cukai (Langkawi) Tahun 2016"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2016","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2016_P.U.(A)283-2016_EXCISE DUTIES (LANGKAWI) ORDER 2016.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3759-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Duti Eksais (Langkawi) 2016.\n\n (2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 November 2016.\n\nDuti-duti Eksais"}},{"id":"MY-H3759-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Duti-duti eksais hendaklah dikenakan ke atas dan dibayar oleh pengimport\n\nberkenaan dengan liquor yang memabukkan, produk tembakau dan rokok yang\n\ndiimport ke dalam Langkawi mengikut kadar-kadar yang dinyatakan dalam ruang 4\n\nJadual kepada Perintah Duti Eksais yang sedang berkuat kuasa.\n\nDibuat 31 Oktober 2016\n\n[SULIT KE.HT(96)669/12-127 Sk. 10; Perb. CR(8.20)116/1-138(2016)(SJ.8)(SK.1);\n\nPN(PU2)337]\n\nDATUK JOHARI BIN ABDUL GHANI\n\nMenteri Kewangan Kedua\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut subseksyen 91DA(2) Akta Eksais 1976]\n\nEXCISE ACT 1976\n\nEXCISE DUTIES (LANGKAWI) ORDER 2016\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 91DA(1)(a) of the\n\nExcise Act 1976 [Act 176], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H376"] = {"id":"MY-H376","coverage":"partial","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-detail.php?act=481&lang=BI","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":27,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"1992年马来西亚旅游促进局法","en":"MALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD ACT 1992","orig":"MALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD ACT 1992","vi":"Luật về Ủy ban Xúc tiến Du lịch Malaysia năm 1992","th":"พระราชบัญญัติคณะกรรมการส่งเสริมการท่องเที่ยวมาเลเซีย ค.ศ. 1992","id":"Undang-Undang Dewan Promosi Pariwisata Malaysia Tahun 1992","ms":"Akta Lembaga Penggalakan Pelancongan Malaysia 1992"},"level":"law","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"ACT481","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"1992","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 31 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\1992_481_MALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD ACT 1992.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H376-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"chapter":{"en":"Part I"},"text":{"en":"1. (1) This Act may be cited as the Malaysia Tourism Short title\nPromotion Board Act 1992.                       —\n\n(2) This Act shall come into force on such date as the\nMinister may, by notification in the Gazette, appoint.\n\nment."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"chapter":{"en":"Part I"},"text":{"en":"2. (1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise Interpretation.\nrequires—\n\n\"appointed day\" means the day appointed by the\nMinister under section 1;\n\n\"Board\" means the Malaysia Tourism Promotion\nBoard established under section 3;\n\n\"Chairman\" means the Chairman of the Board\nappointed under section 5;\n\n\"Commissioner of Tourism\" means the Commissioner\nof Tourism appointed under section 4 of the Tourism\nIndustry Act 1992;                             Act 482.\n\n(Pt. I-III, S. 2-3]\n\nAct 72.\n\nEstablishment\nof the Board.\n\n6                     Act 481\n\n\"Corporation\" means the Tourist Development\nCorporation of Malaysia established under the Tourist\nDevelopment Corporation of Malaysia Act 1972;\n\n\"Deputy Chairman\" means the Deputy Chairman\nappointed under section 5;\n\n\"Deputy Director General\" means a Deputy Director\nGeneral appointed under section 10;\n\n\"Director\" means a Director appointed under section\n10;\n\n\"Director General\" means the Director General\nappointed under section 10;\n\n\"Fund\" means the fund established under section 14;\n\n\"Minister\" means the Minister for the time being\ncharged with the responsibility for tourism;\n\n\"repealed Act\" means the Tourist Development\nCorporation of Malaysia Act 1972 and includes any\nregulations made thereunder;\n\n\"tourism enterprise\" has the same meaning assigned\nto it under the Tourism Industry Act 1992.\n\n(2) Any reference in this Act to \"this Act\" shall,\nunless otherwise expressly stated, be deemed to include\na reference to any regulations, rules order, notification\nor other subsidiary legislation made under this Act.\n\nPart II\n\nTHE MALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD"}},{"id":"MY-H376-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"3. There is hereby established a body corporate by the\nname of \"Malaysia Tourism Promotion Board\" with\nperpetual succession and a common seal, which may\nsue and be sued in its name and, subject to and for the\npurposes of this Act, may enter into contracts and may\nacquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and\n\n(Pt. II, S.\n\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD     7\n\nimmovable property of every description and may\nconvey, assign, surrender, yield up, charge, mortgage,\ndemise, reassign, transfer or otherwise dispose of, or\ndeal with any movable or immovable property or any\ninterest therein vested in the Board upon such terms as\nit deems fit."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"4. (1) The functions of the Board shall be—\n\n(a) to stimulate and promote tourism to and within\nMalaysia;\n\n(b) to stimulate, promote and market, inter-\nnationally and locally, Malaysia as a tourist\ndestination;\n\n(c) to coordinate any marketing or promotion\nactivity in relation to tourism conducted by any\ngovernment department or governmental or\nnon-governmental agencies or organisations;\nand\n\n(d) to make recommendations to the Minister as to\nthe methods, measures and programmes to be\nadopted to facilitate and stimulate the\ndevelopment and promotion of the tourism\nindustry in Malaysia and where approved by\nthe Minister, to implement or assist in the\nimplementation of the methods, measures and\nprogrammes in question.\n\n(2) The Board shall have power to do all things\nexpedient or reasonably necessary for, or incidental to,\nthe performance of its functions, and in particular, but\nwithout prejudice to the generality of the foregoing—\n\n(a) to carry on all activities relating to tourism\nwhich are commercial or industrial in nature\nand activities of research and training, the\ncarrying on whereof appears to it to be\nrequisite, advantageous or convenient for or in\nconnection with the performance of its\nfunctions;\n\n3-4]\n\nFunctions\nand powers of\nthe Board.\n\n(Pt. II, S. 41\n\n(b)\n\n(c)\n\n(d)\n\n(e)\n\n(f)\n\n(g)\n\n(h)\n\nAct 481\n\nto co-operate with or act as agent of, or\notherwise act in association with or on behalf\nof any agency or organisation, international or\notherwise;\n\nto secure local and overseas publicity for the\npromotion of Malaysia as a tourist destination;\n\nto promote and co-ordinate the carrying on of\nsuch activities which are connected or related\nto its functions by any government department,\nor governmental or non-governmental agency\nor organisation;\n\nto conduct researches, surveys and inves-\ntigations which are requisite, advantageous or\nconvenient for or in connection with the\nperformance of its functions;\n\nto require any government department, or\ngovernmental or non-governmental agency\nor organisation to submit information,\nprogrammes and reports in respect of its\ntourism promotion and marketing activities;\n\nto enter into such negotiations and\narrangements as the Board considers necessary\nfor the performance of its functions;\n\nto assist in the development of tourism\nenterprises in Malaysia, and in the provision\nor improvement of tourist facilities and\nattractions in Malaysia;\n\nto give assistance to any governmental or non-\ngovernmental agency or organisation\nappearing to the Board to have facilities for\nthe carrying on of any such activities,\nincluding, with the approval of the Minister,\nfinancial assistance by the taking up of share\nor loan capital or by loan or otherwise;\n\n(Pt. II, S. 4-5)\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD     9\n\n(j) to dispose of capital assets and to use the\nproceeds from such disposal as the Board\ndeems fit;\n\n(k) to appoint such agents as it may deem fit for\nthe purpose of performing its functions;\n\n(1) to impose fees or any other charges it deems\nfit for giving effect to any of its functions or\npowers;\n\n(m) to do such other things as it deems fit to enable\nit to carry out its functions and powers\neffectively; and\n\n(n) to exercise all powers and perform all duties\nwhich, under or by virtue of any other written\nlaw, may be vested or delegated to it."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"5. (1) The Board shall consist of the following Membership\n\nmembers who shall be appointed by the Minister:    hee\n\n(a) a Chairman;\n(b) a Deputy Chairman;\n(c) the Director General; and\n\n(d) not less than six but not more than ten\nmembers of whom—\n\n(i) at least four shall be persons who are\nconnected with any tourism enterprise\nbut shall not hold any public office;\n\n(ii) at least two shall be representatives of\nthe Ministry of Culture, Arts and\nTourism and the Ministry of Finance\nrespectively; and\n\n(iii) any other persons as the Minister\nconsiders fit and proper to be members\nof the Board.\n\n(Pt. I, S. 5-9]\n\nPublic\nAuthorities\nProtection\nAct 1948.\nAct 198.\n\nPublic\nservants.\n\nFMS.\nCap. 45.\n\nPower of the\nMinister to\ngive\ndirections.\n\nReports and\ninformation.\n\n10                    Act 481\n\n(2) The Minister shall appoint the Chairman and the\nDeputy Chairman from amongst persons who in the\nopinion of the Minister has had extensive experience in\ntourism enterprises or in other fields of activities which\nis of great service to the development of tourism.\n\n(3) The Board may delegate any of its functions and\npowers to the Chairman.\n\n(4) The provisions of the Schedule shall apply to the\nBoard."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"6. The Public Authorities Protection Act 1948 shall\napply to any action, suit, prosecution or proceedings\nagainst the Board or any member, officer, servant or\nagent of the Board in respect of any act, neglect or\ndefault done or committed by him in such capacity."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"7. All members, officers and servants of the Board,\nwhile discharging their duties as such members, officers\nand servants, shall be deemed to be public servants\nwithin the meaning of the Penal Code."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"8. The Board shall be responsible to the Minister, and\nthe Minister may from time to time give directions not\ninconsistent with the provisions of this Act and the\nBoard shall give effect to all such directions."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"9. (1) The Board shall furnish to the Minister such\ninformation with respect to its property and activities as\nthe Minister may from time to time require or direct.\n\n(2) The Board shall, not later than the 30th day of\nJune of each year, cause to be made and transmitted to\nthe Minister a report dealing with the activities of the\nBoard during the preceding year and the report shall\ncontain such information relating to the proceedings and\npolicy of the Board as the Minister may from time to\ntime specify.\n\n(Pt. III, S. 10]\n\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD     11\n\nPART III\n\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, DEPUTY DIRECTOR GENERALS,\nDIRECTORS AND OTHER OFFICERS AND SERVANTS"}},{"id":"MY-H376-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"10. (1) The Minister shall appoint a fit and proper Appointment\n\nperson, on such terms and conditions as he may\ndetermine, to be the Director General who shall be the\nchief executive officer of the Board.\n\n(2) The Board shall—\n\n(a) with the approval of the Minister, appoint such\nnumber of Deputy Director Generals and\nDirectors as it deems appropriate; and\n\n(b) appoint such other officers and servants as it\nconsiders necessary for the efficient conduct\nof the business of the Board,\n\non such terms and conditions, including remuneration,\nas may be determined by the Board with the approval\nof the Minister.\n\n(3) The Director General shall, subject to the\ndirection of the Board on matters of policy, be charged\nwith the day to day administration and management of\nthe affairs of the Board.\n\n(4) The Director General shall be responsible to the\nChairman acting on behalf of the Board.\n\n(5) The Director General shall have the general\ncontrol of the Deputy Director Generals, Directors and\nother officers and servants of the Board.\n\n(6) The Board may, with the approval of the Minister,\nvest the Director General, the Deputy Director Generals\nand the Directors with such powers and impose upon\nthem such duties as may be determined by the Board.\n\n(7) The Director General, Deputy Director Generals\nand Directors shall perform such further duties as the\nBoard may from time to time direct.\n\nof the\nDirector\nGeneral,\nDeputy\nDirector\nGenerals,\nDirectors\nand other\nofficers\n\nand servants.\n\n(Pt. III, S. 10-13)\n12                     Act 481\n\n(8) If the Director General is temporarily absent from\nMalaysia or is temporarily incapacitated through illness\nor for any other sufficient reason from the performance\nof his duties, the Board may direct any Deputy Director\nGeneral to perform his duties during such temporary\nabsence or incapacity.\n\nIneligibility 11. No person shall be eligible for employment as an\nean  officer or servant of the Board if he has, directly or\n\nindirectly, by himself or his partner, any share or\ninterest in any contract or proposed contract with, for\nor on behalf of the Board.\n\nRegulations 12. The Board may, from time to time, with the\nwith respect                 SEN               :     :\n\nto conditions 2PProval of the Minister, make regulations with respect\nof service. | to the conditions of service of its officers and servants.\n\nss eee  B. (1) The Board may, from time to time, with the\nto discintine. approval of the Minister, make regulations with respect\nto the discipline of its officers and servants.\n\n(2) The regulations made under this section may\ninclude provisions for—\n\n(a) the interdiction with reduction in salary or in\nother remuneration; or\n\n(b) the suspension without salary or other\nremuneration,\n\nof an officer or servant of the Board during the pendency\nof disciplinary proceedings.\n\n(3) The regulations made under this section shall\ncreate such disciplinary offences and provide for such\ndisciplinary punishments as the Board may deem\nappropriate, and the punishments so provided may\nextend to dismissal or reduction in rank.\n\n(4) The regulations made under this section shall, in\nprescribing the procedure for disciplinary proceedings,\nprovide for an opportunity for representations to be\nmade by the person against whom the disciplinary\n\n(Pt. I-IV, S. 13-15]\n\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD    13\n\nproceedings are taken before a decision is arrived at by\nthe Board on the disciplinary charge laid against such\nperson.\n\nPART IV\nFINANCE"}},{"id":"MY-H376-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"14. (1) There is hereby established, for the purposes of\nthis Act, a fund to be administered and controlled by the\nBoard.\n\n(2) The Fund shall consist of—\n\n(a) such sums as may be provided from time to\ntime by Parliament;\n\n(b) such sums as may be paid from time to time\nto the Board from loans made by the Board;\n\n(c) monies earned by the operation of any project,\nscheme or enterprise financed from the Fund;\n\n(d) monies earned or arising from any property,\ninvestments, mortgages, charges or debentures\nacquired by or vested in the Board;\n\n(e) any property, investments, mortgages, charges\nor debentures acquired by or vested in the\nBoard;\n\n(f) sums borrowed by the Board for the purposes\nof meeting any of its obligations or discharging\nany of its duties; and\n\n(g) all other sums or property which may in any\nmanner become payable to or vested in the\nBoard in respect of any matter incidental to its\nfunctions, powers and duties.\n\n5. It shall be the duty of the Board to conserve the\nFund by so performing, exercising and discharging its\nfunctions, powers and duties under this Act as to secure\nthat the total revenues of the Board are, subject to any\ndirections given by the Minister, sufficient to meet all\n\nThe Fund.\n\nConservation\nof Fund.\n\n(Pt. IV, S. 15-17)\n\nExpenditure\nto be\ncharged on\nthe Fund.\n\nExpenditure\nand\npreparation\nof estimates.\n\n14                     Act 481\n\nsums properly chargeable to its revenue account,\nincluding depreciation and interest on capital, taking one\nyear with another."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"16. The Fund shall be expended for the purpose of—\n\n(a) paying any expenditure lawfully incurred by\nthe Board, including legal fees and other fees\nand costs, and the remuneration of officers and\nservants appointed and employed by the\nBoard, including superannuation allowances,\npensions and gratuities;\n\n(b) paying any other expenses, costs or\nexpenditure properly incurred or accepted by\nthe Board in the performance of its functions\nor the exercise of its powers under section 4;\n\n(c) purchasing or hiring equipment, machinery,\nstores and any other materials, acquiring land\nand erecting buildings, and carrying out any\nother works and undertakings in the\nperformance of its functions or the exercise of\nits powers under section 4;\n\n(d) repaying any monies borrowed under this Act\nand the interest due thereon; and\n\n(e) generally, paying any expenses for carrying\ninto effect the provisions of this Act."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"17. (1) The expenditure of the Board up to such amount\nas may be authorised by the Minister for any one year\nshall be defrayed out of the Fund.\n\n(2) Before the beginning of September of each year,\nthe Board shall submit to the Minister an estimate of the\nexpenditure for the following year in such form and\ncontaining such particulars as the Minister may direct;\nand the Minister shall, before the beginning of the\nfollowing year, notify the Board of the amount\nauthorised for expenditure generally or the amounts\nauthorised for each description of expenditure.\n\n(Pt. IV-V, S. 17-22]\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD     15\n\n(3) The Board may at any time submit to the Minister\na supplementary estimate for any one year and the\nMinister may allow the whole or any part of the\nadditional expenditure included therein."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"18. The provisions of the Statutory Bodies (Accounts Statutory\nand Annual Reports) Act 1980 shall apply to the Board. Bodies\n\n(Account and\nAnnual\nReports) Act\n\nOTHER POWERS OF THE BOARD"}},{"id":"MY-H376-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"19. The Board may, by an instrument in writing under Delegation\nthe common seal, delegate to any person or body such a\nof its duties as may be necessary to be performed in or\n\noutside Malaysia:\n\nProvided that any such person or body shall have no\ncontrol over the Fund and shall act in all respects in\naccordance with the direction of the Board."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"20. The Board may, from time to time, with the Power to\napproval of the Minister, borrow, at such rate of interest °°\":\nand for such period and upon such terms as to the time\n\nand method of repayment and otherwise as the Minister\n\nmay approve, any sums required by the Board for\nmeeting any of its obligations or discharging any of its\n\nduties."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"21. The assets of the Board shall, in so far as they are Investment.\nnot required to be expended by the Board under this\n\nAct, be invested in such manner as the Minister may\napprove."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"22. The Board may employ and pay agents and Power to\ntechnical advisers, including advocates and solicitors, *™ply-\nbankers, stockbrokers, surveyors, valuers and other\npersons, to transact any business or to do any act\nrequired to be transacted or done in the performance of\n\nits functions, the exercise of its powers or the discharge\n\nof its duties or for the better carrying into effect the\npurposes of this Act.\n\n(Pt. VI, S. 23-241\n\nObligation\nof secrecy.\n\nPower to\nmake\nregulations.\n\n16                   Act 481\n\nPART VI\nGENERAL"}},{"id":"MY-H376-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"23. (1) Except for any of the purposes of this Act or\nfor any civil or criminal proceedings under any written\nlaw, no member, officer or servant of the Board shall\ndisclose any information which has been obtained by\nhim in the course of his duties and which is not\npublished in pursuance of this Act.\n\n(2) Any person contravening subsection (1) shall be\nguilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction\nto imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or\nto a fine not exceeding five thousand ringgit or to both."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"24. (1) The Board may, with the approval of the\nMinister, make such regulations as may be expedient or\nnecessary for the better carrying out of the provisions\nof this Act.\n\n(2) Without prejudice to the generality of subsection\n(1), regulations may be made for—\n\n(a) prescribing the manner in which documents,\ncheques and instruments of any description\nshall be signed or executed on behalf of the\nBoard;\n\n(b) prescribing the responsibilities and control of\nofficers and servants of the Board;\n\n(c) imposing fees in such cases as may be\ndetermined by the Board;\n\n(d) providing generally for the performance of the\nfunctions, the exercise of the powers and the\ndischarge of the duties of the Board under the\nprovisions of this Act.\n\n(3) Regulations under this section—\n\n(a) may provide that any act or omission in\ncontravention of any provision thereof shall be\nan offence; and\n\n(Pt. VI-VII, S. 24-27]\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD     17\n\n(b) may provide for the imposition of penalties for\nsuch offence, which penalties shall not exceed\nfive thousand ringgit or one year's imprison-\nment or both.\n\nPART VII\n\nREPEAL AND TRANSITIONAL PROVISIONS"}},{"id":"MY-H376-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"25. The Tourist Development Corporation of Malaysia Repeal.\nAct 1972 and any regulations made thereunder are 4%\"\nhereby repealed."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"26. (1) The members of the Board of Management of Continuance\nthe Corporation appointed under section 5 of the Se aa\nrepealed Act shall, on the appointed day, be members of Manage-\nof the Board and shall be subject to all the provisions mem and\n\nd               \"                                               officers and\nof this Act relating to such members and shall be servants.\n\ndeemed to have been appointed under this Act.\n\n(2) Every person who immediately before the\nappointed day was employed as an officer or servant of\nthe Corporation shall on that day be deemed to be\nemployed as such officer or servant, as the case may be,\nof the Board upon the same terms and conditions of\nservice as before the appointed day.\n\n(3) All disciplinary proceedings which, immediately\nbefore the appointed day, were pending against any\nofficer or servant of the Corporation on or after that\nday, may be continued against the officer or servant by\nthe appropriate authority of the Board."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"27. (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, all monies Transfer of\n\nstanding in, and due to be paid to, the fund set up under [\"® *s*ts:\n-                                               .           property,\n\nsection 8 of the repealed Act shall on the appointed day rights,\n\nbe transferred to the Fund.                        a\n\nobligations.\n\n(2) All assets, property, rights, liabilities and\nobligations which immediately before the appointed day\nwere those of the Corporation shall as from that day\ndevolve on the Board.            |\n\n(Pt. VII, S. 28-291\n\nConstruction.\n\nContinuance\nof laws, etc.\n\n18                 Act 481"}},{"id":"MY-H376-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"28. All references in any other written law to the\nCorporation shall be construed as references to—\n\n(a) in the case of matters relating to licensing or\nregistration, the Commissioner of Tourism;\nand\n\n(b) in any other case, the Board."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"29. (1) All orders, regulations, directions, appoint-\nments, notifications, exemptions and approvals made or\ngiven under, or in accordance with, or by virtue of, the\nrepealed Act shall, in so far as they are not inconsistent\nwith the provisions of this Act or the Tourism Industry\nAct 1992, be deemed to have been made or given under\nthis Act or the Tourism Industry Act 1992 and shall\ncontinue in force until other provisions shall be made\nunder this Act or the Tourism Industry Act 1992 or until\nthe date upon which they expire.\n\n(2) Any application for a licence or certificate of\nregistration, approval or consent, or for any purpose\nwhatsoever, or any appeal, made by any person to the\nMinister or the Corporation before the appointed day,\nand pending immediately before such day, shall, if there\nis a corresponding provision under this Act or the\nTourism Industry Act 1992 be dealt with as if made\nunder that provision, and if there is no such\ncorresponding provision, such application or appeal\nshall lapse on the appointed day.\n\n(3) Any licence or certificate of registration granted\nunder the repealed Act shall be deemed to be a licence\nor certificate of registration granted under the Tourism\nIndustry Act 1992 and shall remain valid for a period\nof six months from the appointed day and be subject to\nthe provisions of the said Act applicable to a licence or\na certificate of registration or any other condition,\nlimitation' or restriction that may be imposed as if it\nwere a licence or certificate of registration granted under\nthat Act.\n\n(Pt. VII, S. 29-31]\n\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD     19\n\n(4) All transactions or dealings lawfully entered into\nor executed, and all business lawfully done, under or in\naccordance with the repealed Act by any person who is\nlicensed or registered or deemed to be licensed or\nregistered under the Tourism Industry Act 1992, shall\nbe deemed to have been lawfully and validly entered\ninto, executed or done, under and in accordance with\nthe Tourism Industry Act 1992, and accordingly any\nright or liability under such transaction, dealing or\nbusiness existing immediately before the appointed day,\nshall be deemed to continue to be lawful and valid under\nthe Tourism Industry Act 1992."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"30. All deeds, bonds, agreements, instruments and\nworking arrangements subsisting immediately before the\nappointed day shall be in full force and effect against\nor in favour of the Board and enforceable as fully and\neffectually as if, instead of the Corporation, or any\nperson acting on behalf of the Corporation, the Board\nhad been named therein or had been a party thereto."}},{"id":"MY-H376-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"31. (1) The repeal of the repealed Act shall not affect\nany person's liability to be prosecuted or punished for\noffences committed under the repealed Act before the\nappointed day, or any proceedings brought or sentence\nimposed before that day in respect of such offence.\n\n(2) Any proceedings, whether civil or criminal, or\ncause of action pending or existing immediately before\nthe appointed day by or against the Corporation may be\ncontinued or instituted by or against the Board or the\nCommissioner of Tourism, as the case may be, as it\nmight have been by or against the Corporation as if this\nAct or the Tourism Industry Act 1992 had not been\npassed.\n\n(3) Any appeal brought or any leave to appeal applied\non or after the appointed day against a decision given\nin any legal proceedings before that day may be brought\nby or against the Board or the Commissioner of\nTourism, as the case may be, as it might have been\nbrought by or against the Corporation as if this Act or\nthe Tourism Industry Act 1992 had not been passed.\n\nExisting\ncontracts.\n\nContinuance\nof criminal\nand civil\nproceedings.\n\n(Pt. VII, S. 32, Schedule]\n20                          Act 481\n\nPrevention 32, (1) If any difficulty arises in respect to the\n\nof anomalies: foregoing transitional provisions of this Act the Minister\nmay, by order, make such modifications in those\nprovisions as may appear to him necessary for\npreventing anomalies:\n\nProvided that the Minister shall not exercise the\npowers conferred by this section after the expiration of\ntwo years from the appointed day.\n\n(2) In this section, \"modifications\" includes\namendments, additions, deletions, substitutions,\nadaptations, variations, alterations and non-application\nof any provision of this Part.\n\nSCHEDULE\n(Subsection 5(4))\n\nAppointment,    1. (1) A member of the Board, other than the Director General,\na   shall, subject to such conditions of appointment, hold office for a\n\nterm not exceeding three years and is eligible for reappointment.\n\n(2) The appointment of any member may at any time be revoked\nby the Minister without assigning any reason therefor.\n\n(3) A member, other than the Director General, may at any time\nresign his office by letter addressed to the Minister.\n\n(4) The Director General may at any time resign his office by\nletter addressed to the Board and to the Minister in accordance with\nthe terms and conditions of service applicable to his case.\n\n(5) Every member shall devote such time to the business of the\nBoard as is necessary to discharge his duties effectively.\n\nVacation of     2. (1) The office of a member of the Board shall be vacated—\noffice.\n(a) if he dies;\n\n(b) if there has been proved against him, or he has been\nconvicted on, a charge in respect of—\n\n(i) an offence involving fraud, dishonesty or moral\nturpitude;\n\n(ii) an offence under any law relating to corruption or\nunder section 23; or\n\n(iii) any other offence punishable with imprisonment (in\nitself only or in addition to or in lieu of a fine) for\nmore than two years;\n\n(Schedule)\n\nMALAYSIA TOURISM PROMOTION BOARD    21\n\n(c) if he becomes bankrupt;\n\n(d) if he is of unsound mind or is otherwise incapable of\ndischarging his duties;\n\n(e) if he absents himself from three consecutive meetings\nwithout leave of the Board;\n\n(f) in the event of his resignation being accepted by the\nMinister or, in the case of the Director General, by the\nBoard with the approval of the Minister;\n\n(g) if his appointment is revoked by the Minister.\n\n(2) Where any person ceases to be a member by reason of any\nof the provisions of this Act, another person shall be appointed in\nhis place in accordance with the provisions applying.\n\n3. There may be paid to members of the Board such remuneration\nand allowance as the Minister may determine.\n\n4. (1) The Board shall meet at least once in every two months and\nthe Chairman or the Deputy Chairman, where the Chairman is\nabsent, shall have power to convene a meeting of the Board\nwhenever he deems it necessary.\n\n(2) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Board shall\ndetermine its own procedure.\n\n5. The Board may request any person (not being a member of the\nBoard) to attend any meeting or deliberation of the Board for the\npurpose of advising it on any matter under discussion, but any\nperson so attending shall have no right to vote at the said meeting\nor deliberation.\n\n6. (1) The Board shall have a common seal, which shall bear such\ndevice as the Board shall approve and such seal may from time to\ntime be broken, changed altered or made anew as the Board may\nthink fit.\n\n(2) Until a seal is provided by the Board, a stamp bearing the\nwords \"Malaysia Tourism Promotion Board\" may be used and shall\nbe deemed to be the common seal.\n\n(3) The common seal shall be kept in the custody of the\nChairman or such other person as may be authorised by the Board\nand all deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal\nof the Board shall be sealed accordingly in the presence of two\nmembers of the Board who shall sign every such deed, document\nor instrument to which such seal is affixed; and such signing shall\nwithout further attestation be sufficient evidence that such seal was\nduly and properly affixed and that the same is the lawful seal of\nthe Board.\n\nRemuneration.\n\nMecting.\n\nThe Board may\ninvite others to\nmeetings.\n\nCommon seal,\n\n(Schedule)\n\nDisclosure of\ninterest.\n\nMinutes.\n\nValidity of acts\n\nand proceedings.\n\n22                     Act 481\n\n(4) The common seal of the Board shall be officially and\njudicially noticed.\n\n7. A member of the Board having, directly or indirectly, by\nhimself or his partner, any interest in any company or undertaking\nwith which the Board proposes to make any contract or having any\ninterest in any such contract or in any matter under discussion by\nthe Board shall disclose to the Board the fact of his interest and\nthe nature thereof, and such disclosure shall be recorded in the\nminutes of the Board and unless specifically authorised thereto by\nthe Chairman, such member shall take no part in any deliberation\nor decision of the Board relating to the contract or matter.\n\n8. (1) The Board shall cause minutes of all meetings of the Board\nto be maintained and kept in a proper form.\n\n(2) Any minutes made of meetings of the Board shall, if duly\nsigned, be admissible in evidence in all legal proceedings without\nfurther proof and every meeting of the Board in respect of the\nproceedings of which minutes have been so made shall be deemed\nto have been duly convened and held and all members thereat to\nhave been duly qualified to act.\n\n9. No act done or proceedings taken under this Act shall be\nquestioned on the ground of—\n\n(a) any vacancy in the membership of, or of any defect in\nthe constitution of, the Board;\n\n(b) the contravention by any member of the Board of the\nprovisions of paragraph 7; or\n\n(c) any omission, defect or irregularity not affecting the\nmerits of the case.\n\nDICETAK OLEH GHAZALI BIN JANI, J.S.D., K.M.N., A.M.P., P.P.T.,\nKETUA PENGARAH PERCETAKAN NEGARA, MALAYSIA\nDENGAN PERINTAH PADA 2048 FEBRUARI 1992\n\nHarga: $2.00"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3760"] = {"id":"MY-H3760","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2017&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2017年印刷机与出版物（不良出版物管制）（第32号）令","en":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 32) ORDER 2017","orig":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 32) ORDER 2017","ms":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Kawalan Penerbitan Tidak Diingini) (Bilangan 32) 2017","vi":"Lệnh về Máy in và ấn phẩm (Kiểm soát ấn phẩm không mong muốn) (số 32) năm 2017","th":"คำสั่งแท่นพิมพ์และสิ่งพิมพ์ (การควบคุมสิ่งพิมพ์ที่ไม่พึงประสงค์) (ฉบับที่ 32) ค.ศ. 2017","id":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Pengendalian Terbitan Tidak Diinginkan) (Nomor 32) Tahun 2017"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2017","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2017_P.U.(A)283-2017_PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 32) ORDER 2017.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3760-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan\n\n(Kawalan Hasil Penerbitan Tidak Diingini) (No. 32) 2017.\n\nLarangan"}},{"id":"MY-H3760-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Pencetakan, pengimportan, penghasilan, penghasilan semula, penerbitan,\n\npenjualan, pengeluaran, pengelilingan, pengedaran atau pemilikan hasil penerbitan\n\nyang diperihalkan dalam Jadual yang mungkin memudaratkan ketenteraman awam,\n\nyang mungkin menggemparkan fikiran orang ramai dan yang mungkin memudaratkan\n\nkepentingan awam adalah dilarang secara mutlak di seluruh Malaysia.\n\nJADUAL\n\nTajuk Hasil\n\nPenerbitan\n\nPengarang Penerbit Pencetak Bahasa\n\n1. Wacana\n\nPemikiran\n\nReformis (Jilid I)\n\nAhmad\n\nFarouk Musa\n\nIslamic Renaissance\n\nFront Berhad\n\nLevel 8,\n\nPavilion KL,\n\n168, Jalan\n\nBukit Bintang,\n\n55100 Kuala Lumpur\n\nWilayah Persekutuan\n\nWai Xin Industries\n\nSdn. Bhd.\n\nNo 23 Jalan PBS\n\n14/13\n\nTaman Perindustrian\n\nBukit Serdang\n\n43300 Seri\n\nKembangan\n\nSelangor\n\nMelayu\n\nTajuk Hasil\n\nPenerbitan\n\nPengarang Penerbit Pencetak Bahasa\n\n2. Wacana\n\nPemikiran\n\nReformis\n\n(Jilid II)\n\nAhmad\n\nFarouk Musa\n\nIslamic Renaissance\n\nFront Berhad\n\nLevel 8,\n\nPavilion KL,\n\n168, Jalan\n\nBukit Bintang,\n\n55100, Kuala Lumpur\n\nWilayah Persekutuan\n\nAcademe Art &\n\nPrinting Services\n\nSdn. Bhd.\n\nNo 7, Jalan Rajawali\n\n1A,\n\nBandar Puchong\n\nJaya,\n\nBatu 8,\n\nJalan Puchong,\n\n47100 Selangor\n\nMelayu\n\nDibuat 6 September 2017\n\n[KDN.PQ.S. 600-16/15/51; PN(PU2)417/XXII]\n\nDATO' SERI DR. AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\n\nMenteri Dalam Negeri\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS ACT 1984\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS\n\n(CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 32) ORDER 2017\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 7(1) of the\n\nPrinting Presses and Publications Act 1984 [Act 301], the Minister makes the\n\nfollowing order:\n\nCitation\n\n1. This order may be cited as the Printing Presses and Publications\n\n(Control of Undesirable Publications) (No. 32) Order 2017.\n\nProhibition\n\n2. The printing, importation, production, reproduction, publishing, sale, issue,\n\ncirculation, distribution or possession of the publication described in the Schedule\n\nwhich is likely to be prejudicial to public order, which is likely to alarm public opinion and\n\nwhich is prejudicial to public interest is absolutely prohibited throughout Malaysia.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nTitle of\n\nPublication\n\nAuthor Publisher Printer Language\n\n1. Wacana Pemikiran\n\nReformis (Jilid I)\n\nAhmad\n\nFarouk Musa\n\nIslamic\n\nRenaissance Front\n\nBerhad\n\nLevel 8,\n\nPavilion KL,\n\n168, Jalan\n\nBukit Bintang,\n\n55100 Kuala\n\nLumpur\n\nWilayah\n\nPersekutuan\n\nWai Xin\n\nIndustries Sdn.\n\nBhd.\n\nNo 23 Jalan PBS\n\n14/13\n\nTaman\n\nPerindustrian\n\nBukit Serdang\n\n43300 Seri\n\nKembangan\n\nSelangor\n\nMalay\n\nTitle of\n\nPublication\n\nAuthor Publisher Printer Language\n\n2. Wacana Pemikiran\n\nReformis (Jilid II)\n\nAhmad\n\nFarouk Musa\n\nIslamic\n\nRenaissance Front\n\nBerhad\n\nLevel 8,\n\nPavilion KL,\n\n168, Jalan\n\nBukit Bintang,\n\n55100, Kuala\n\nLumpur\n\nWilayah\n\nPersekutuan\n\nAcademe Art &\n\nPrinting Services\n\nSdn. Bhd.\n\nNo 7, Jalan\n\nRajawali 1A,\n\nBandar Puchong\n\nJaya,\n\nBatu 8,\n\nJalan Puchong,\n\n47100 Selangor\n\nMalay\n\nMade 6 September 2017\n\n[KDN.PQ.S. 600-16/15/51; PN(PU2)417/XXII]\n\nDATO' SERI DR. AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\n\nMinister of Home Affairs"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3761"] = {"id":"MY-H3761","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2018&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2018年供应管制（管制物品）（第4号）令","en":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2018","orig":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2018","ms":"Perintah Kawalan Bekalan (Barang Kawalan) (Bilangan 4) 2018","vi":"Lệnh về Kiểm soát nguồn cung (Hàng hóa được kiểm soát) (số 4) năm 2018","th":"คำสั่งการควบคุมเสบียง (สิ่งของควบคุม) (ฉบับที่ 4) ค.ศ. 2018","id":"Perintah Pengendalian Persediaan (Barang yang Dikendalikan) (Nomor 4) Tahun 2018"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2018","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2018_P.U.(A)283-2018_CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2018.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3761-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kawalan Bekalan\n\n(Barang-Barang Kawalan) (No. 4) 2018.\n\nBarang-barang kawalan"}},{"id":"MY-H3761-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Barang-barang yang dinyatakan dalam Jadual diisytiharkan sebagai barang-barang\n\nkawalan bagi tempoh dari 3 November 2018 hingga 9 November 2018.\n\nJADUAL\n\nBARANG-BARANG KAWALAN\n\n1. Daging kambing tempatan bertulang\n\n2. Daging kambing dan bebiri import bertulang\n\n3. Tomato\n\n4. Cili merah\n\n5. Kacang dal (Australia)\n\nDibuat 31 Oktober 2018\n\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)0.5001/4 Jld. 8; PN(PU2)188/VIII]\n\nDATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\nMenteri Perdagangan Dalam Negeri\n\ndan Hal Ehwal Pengguna\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES ACT 1961\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2018\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 5 of the\n\nControl of Supplies Act 1961 [Act 122], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation\n\n1. This order may be cited as the Control of Supplies (Controlled Articles)\n\n(No. 4) Order 2018.\n\nControlled articles\n\n2. The articles specified in the Schedule are declared to be controlled articles for the\n\nperiod from 3 November 2018 to 9 November 2018.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nCONTROLLED ARTICLES\n\n1. Local bone-in mutton\n\n2. Imported bone-in mutton\n\n3. Tomato\n\n4. Red chilli\n\n5. Dal (Australia)\n\nMade 31 October 2018\n\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)0.5001/4 Jld. 8; PN(PU2)188/XXIII]\n\nDATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\nMinister of Domestic Trade\n\nand Consumer Affairs"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3762"] = {"id":"MY-H3762","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2019&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2019年供应管制（管制物品）（第4号）令","en":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2019","orig":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2019","ms":"Perintah Kawalan Bekalan (Barang Kawalan) (Bilangan 4) 2019","vi":"Lệnh về Kiểm soát nguồn cung (Hàng hóa được kiểm soát) (số 4) năm 2019","th":"คำสั่งการควบคุมเสบียง (สิ่งของควบคุม) (ฉบับที่ 4) ค.ศ. 2019","id":"Perintah Pengendalian Persediaan (Barang yang Dikendalikan) (Nomor 4) Tahun 2019"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2019","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2019_P.U.(A)283-2019_CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2019.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3762-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kawalan Bekalan\n\n(Barang-Barang Kawalan) (No. 4) 2019.\n\nBarang-barang kawalan"}},{"id":"MY-H3762-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Barang-barang yang dinyatakan dalam Jadual diisytiharkan sebagai\n\nbarang-barang kawalan bagi tempoh dari 20 Oktober 2019 hingga 2 November 2019.\n\nJADUAL\n\nBARANG-BARANG KAWALAN\n\n1. Daging kambing tempatan bertulang\n\n2. Daging kambing dan bebiri import bertulang\n\n3. Tomato\n\n4. Cili merah\n\n5. Cili kering\n\n6. Kubis bulat import (Indonesia dan China, tidak termasuk kubis Beijing)\n\n7. Bendi\n\n8. Kacang dal (Australia)\n\nDibuat 14 Oktober 2019\n\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)0.5001/4 Jld. 8; PN(PU2)188/XI]\n\nDATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\nMenteri Perdagangan Dalam Negeri\n\ndan Hal Ehwal Pengguna\n\nD\n\nA\n\nT\n\nO\n\n'\n\nS\n\nR\n\nI\n\nH\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES ACT 1961\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 4) ORDER 2019\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 5 of the\n\nControl of Supplies Act 1961 [Act 122], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation\n\n1. This order may be cited as the Control of Supplies (Controlled Articles)\n\n(No. 4) Order 2019.\n\nControlled articles\n\n2. The articles specified in the Schedule are declared to be controlled articles for\n\nthe period from 20 October 2019 to 2 November 2019.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nCONTROLLED ARTICLES\n\n1. Local bone-in mutton\n\n2. Imported bone-in mutton\n\n3. Tomato\n\n4. Red chilli\n\n5. Dried chilli\n\n6. Imported round cabbage (Indonesia and China, not including Beijing\n\ncabbage)\n\n7. Lady's finger\n\n8. Dal (Australia)\n\nMade 14 October 2019\n\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)0.5001/4 Jld. 8; PN(PU2)188/XI]\n\nDATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\nMinister of Domestic Trade\n\nand Consumer Affairs"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3763"] = {"id":"MY-H3763","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2020&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2020年道路交通（禁止使用道路）（联邦道路）（第9号）令","en":"ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD) (FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 9) ORDER 2020","orig":"ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD) (FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 9) ORDER 2020","ms":"Perintah Pengangkutan Jalan (Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Raya Persekutuan) (Bilangan 9) 2020","vi":"Lệnh về Vận tải đường bộ (Cấm sử dụng đường bộ) (Đường bộ liên bang) (số 9) năm 2020","th":"คำสั่งการขนส่งทางถนน (การห้ามใช้ถนน) (ทางหลวงสหพันธ์) (ฉบับที่ 9) ค.ศ. 2020","id":"Perintah Angkutan Jalan (Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Raya Federal) (Nomor 9) Tahun 2020"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2020","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）；已清除正文中的 1 个控制字符（C0/C1 区，法律文本中无合法用途，系 PDF 抽取/表单域残留）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2020_P.U.(A)283-2020_ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD) (FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 9) ORDER 2020.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3763-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Pengangkutan Jalan\n\n(Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Persekutuan) (No. 9) 2020.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 30 September 2020.\n\nLarangan"}},{"id":"MY-H3763-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Pemanduan kenderaan di atas bahagian jalan yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (1)\n\nJadual Pertama sebagaimana yang ditunjukkan dalam peta dalam Jadual Kedua,\n\nmelainkan di atas jalan arah yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (2) Jadual Pertama,\n\nbagi tempoh yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (3) Jadual Pertama, dilarang.\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n\n(1)\n\nJalan yang baginya Larangan\n\nTerpakai\n\n (2)\n\nJalan Arah\n\n(3)\n\nTempoh Larangan\n\nSebahagian Laluan 59, Jalan\n\nTapah-Cameron Highlands\n\nbermula dari seksyen 2.80\n\nhingga seksyen 3.20\n\nsebagaimana yang\n\nditunjukkan dalam peta\n\ndalam Jadual Kedua\n\nKenderaan dari Tapah\n\nke Cameron Highlands dan\n\nsebaliknya hendaklah\n\nmenggunakan jalan lencongan\n\nsementara sebagaimana yang\n\nditunjukkan dalam peta dalam\n\nJadual Kedua\n\n30 September 2020\n\nhingga 2 Julai 2022\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n\nDibuat 29 September 2020\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/6/15 Jld.8; PN(PU2)460/XCVIII]\n\n DATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\n Menteri Kanan Kerja Raya\n\nSg. Karma\n\nseksyen 3.20\n\nRinglet\n\n59 seksyen 2.80\n\nPETUNJUK :\n\nJALAN YANG BAGINYA PERINTAH LARANGAN TERPAKAI\n\nTapah JALAN LENCONGAN SEMENTARA\n\nROAD TRANSPORT ACT 1987\n\nROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD)\n\n(FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 9) ORDER 2020\n\nWHEREAS by P.U. (B) 466/2020 published on 15 September 2020, notice was given of\n\nthe intention to make an order under section 70 of the Road Transport Act 1987\n\n[Act 333]:\n\nAND WHEREAS no objection was received by the Senior Minister of Works\n\nagainst the making of such order:\n\nNOW THEREFORE, in exercise of the powers conferred by section 70 of the Act,\n\nthe Senior Minister of Works, after taking into consideration the matters referred to in\n\nsubsection 70(2) of the Act, makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) This order may be cited as the Road Transport (Prohibition of Use\n\nof Road) (Federal Roads) (No. 9) Order 2020.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 30 September 2020.\n\nProhibition\n\n2. The driving of vehicles on the part of the road as specified in column (1) of the\n\nFirst Schedule as shown on the map in the Second Schedule, otherwise than on the routes\n\nspecified in column (2) of the First Schedule, for the period specified in column (3) of the\n\nFirst Schedule, is prohibited.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\n(1)\n\nRoad to which Prohibition\n\nApplies\n\n(2)\n\nRoutes\n\n(3)\n\nProhibition\n\nPeriod\n\nPart of Route 59, TapahCameron Highlands Road\n\nstarting from section 2.80 to\n\nsection 3.20 as shown on the\n\nmap in the Second Schedule\n\nVehicles from Tapah to\n\nCameron Highlands and\n\nvice versa shall use the\n\ntemporary diversion road as\n\nshown on the map in the\n\nSecond Schedule\n\n30 September 2020\n\nto 2 July 2022\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\nMade 29 September 2020\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/6/15 Jld.8; PN(PU2)460/XCVIII]\n\nDATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\n Senior Minister of Works\n\nLEGEND :\n\nSg. Karma\n\nsection 3.20\n\nRinglet\n\n59 section 2.80\n\nROAD TO WHICH PROHIBITION ORDER IS APPLICABLE\n\nTapah TEMPORARY DIVERSION ROAD"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3764"] = {"id":"MY-H3764","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2021&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2021年所得税（豁免）（第7号）令","en":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) ORDER 2021","orig":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) ORDER 2021","ms":"Perintah Cukai Pendapatan (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 7) 2021","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế thu nhập (Miễn trừ) (số 7) năm 2021","th":"คำสั่งภาษีเงินได้ (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 7) ค.ศ. 2021","id":"Perintah Pajak Penghasilan (Pembebasan) (Nomor 7) Tahun 2021"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2021","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 6 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2021_P.U.(A)283-2021_INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) ORDER 2021.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3764-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Cukai Pendapatan\n(Pengecualian) (No. 7) 2021.\n\n(2) Perintah ini berkuat kuasa mulai tahun taksiran 2021 hingga\ntahun taksiran 2023.\n\nTafsiran"}},{"id":"MY-H3764-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Dalam Perintah ini—\n\n\"pelabur tempatan\" ertinya—\n\n(a) individu warganegara Malaysia dan bermastautin di Malaysia;\n\n(b) syarikat yang seluruh modal syer diterbitkan yang faedahnya dimiliki,\nsecara langsung atau tidak langsung oleh mana-mana orang\nwarganegara Malaysia dan bermastautin di Malaysia; dan\n\n(c) dana amanah yang seluruh kepentingan dalam dana itu yang  faedahnya\ndipegang, secara langsung atau tidak langsung oleh mana -mana orang\nwarganegara Malaysia dan bermastautin di Malaysia yang—\n\n(i) dana itu diwujudkan di Malaysia; dan\n\n(ii) pemegang amanah dana itu adalah warganegara Malaysia dan\nbermastautin di Malaysia;\n\n \"Suruhanjaya Sekuriti Malaysia\" ertinya Suruhanjaya Sekuriti Malaysia yang\nditubuhkan di bawah seksyen 3 Akta Suruhanjaya Sekuriti Malaysia 1993 [Akta 498];\n\n\"syarikat\" ertinya suatu syarikat yang—\n\n(a)  diperbadankan di bawah Akta Syarikat 2016 [Akta 777];\n\n(b)  bermastautin di Malaysia; dan\n\n(c) memegang suatu Lesen Perkhidmatan Pasaran Modal di bawah\nAkta Pasaran Modal dan Perkhidmatan 2007 [ Akta 671 ] untuk\nmenjalankan perniagaan yang disebut dalam subperenggan 3(1).\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H3764-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. (1)  Menteri mengecualikan suatu syarikat daripada pembayaran cukai\npendapatan dalam suatu tempoh asas bagi suatu tahun taksiran berkenaan dengan\npendapatan berkanun  yang diperoleh daripada suatu perniagaan  menyediakan\nperkhidmatan pengurusan kumpulan wang kepada pelabur tempatan di Malaysia.\n\n (2) Pengecualian yang diberikan di bawah subperenggan (1)\nhendaklah tertakluk kepada syarikat mendapatkan perakuan tahunan daripada\nSuruhanjaya Sekuriti Malaysia bahawa syarat yang berikut telah dipenuhi\niaitu syarikat—\n\n(a) menyediakan perkhidmatan pengurusan kumpulan wang\nkepada pelabur tempatan di Malaysia menurut prinsip Syariah;\n\n(b) mempunyai sekurang -kurangnya dua orang pekerja\nsepenuh masa di Malaysia yang salah seorang daripada\npekerja itu memegang suatu Lesen W akil Perkhidmatan\nPasaran Modal di bawah Akta Pasaran Modal dan\nPerkhidmatan 2007; dan\n\n(c) melakukan perbelanjaan operasi tahunan sekurang -kurangnya\ndua ratus lima puluh ribu ringgit (RM250,000.00) di Malaysia.\n\n(3) Tiada apa -apa jua dalam subperenggan (1) boleh  melepaskan atau\ndisifatkan telah melepaskan syarikat itu daripada mematuhi apa -apa kehendak untuk\nmengemukakan apa -apa penyata atau penyata akaun atau memberika n apa -apa\nmaklumat lain di bawah Akta.\n\nAkaun berasingan"}},{"id":"MY-H3764-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Syarikat hendaklah menyenggara suatu akaun berasingan bagi pendapatan\nyang diperoleh daripada perniagaan yang disebut dalam  subperenggan 3(1)\ndalam tempoh asas bagi setiap tahun taksiran dan pendapatan itu hendaklah dikira\nsebagai suatu sumber perniagaan yang berasingan dan berlainan bagi syarikat itu.\n\nPemakaian perenggan 5 dan 6 Jadual 7A kepada Akta"}},{"id":"MY-H3764-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Perenggan 5 dan 6 Jadual 7A kepada Akta hendaklah terpakai, mutatis mutandis,\nbagi amaun pendapatan berkanun yang dikecualikan di bawah subperenggan 3(1).\n\nKetidakpakaian"}},{"id":"MY-H3764-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"ms":"6. Seksyen 60 G Akta tidak terpakai bagi pendapatan berkanun yang dikecualikan\ndi bawah Perintah ini.\n\nDibuat 25 Jun 2021\n[Perb. MOF.TAX(S) 700-3/1/613; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)-71; PN(PU2)/80 Jld. 101]\n\n   TENGKU DATUK SERI UTAMA ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\n                                           Menteri Kewangan\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut subsek syen 127(4) Akta Cukai\nPendapatan 1967]\n\nINCOME TAX ACT 1967\n\nINCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 7) ORDER 2021\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 127(3) (b) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967 [Act 53], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3765"] = {"id":"MY-H3765","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2023&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2023年印刷机与出版物（不良出版物管制）（第4号）令","en":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2023","orig":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2023","ms":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Kawalan Penerbitan Tidak Diingini) (Bilangan 4) 2023","vi":"Lệnh về Máy in và ấn phẩm (Kiểm soát ấn phẩm không mong muốn) (số 4) năm 2023","th":"คำสั่งแท่นพิมพ์และสิ่งพิมพ์ (การควบคุมสิ่งพิมพ์ที่ไม่พึงประสงค์) (ฉบับที่ 4) ค.ศ. 2023","id":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Pengendalian Terbitan Tidak Diinginkan) (Nomor 4) Tahun 2023"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2023","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2023_P.U.(A)283-2023_PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2023.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3765-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan\n\n(Kawalan Hasil Penerbitan Tidak Diingini) (No. 4) 2023.\n\nLarangan"}},{"id":"MY-H3765-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Pencetakan, pengimportan, penghasilan, penghasilan semula, penerbitan,\n\npenjualan, pengeluaran, pengelilingan, pengedaran atau pemilikan hasil penerbitan\n\nyang diperihalkan dalam Jadual yang mungkin memudaratkan kemoralan adalah\n\ndilarang secara mutlak di seluruh Malaysia.\n\nJADUAL\n\n(1)\n\nTajuk Hasil\n\nPenerbitan\n\n(2)\n\nPengarang\n\n(3)\n\nPenerbit\n\n(4)\n\nBahasa\n\nWhen I Was A Kid 3 Cheeming Boey Grey Pigeon\n\nSdn. Bhd.\n\nInggeris\n\nDibuat 15 September 2023\n\n[KDN.PKK.S.600-16/15/123; PN(PU2)417/Jld. 26]\n\n DATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\n Menteri Dalam Negeri\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS ACT 1984\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS\n\n(CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (NO. 4) ORDER 2023\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 7(1) of the\n\nPrinting Presses and Publications Act 1984 [Act 301], the Minister makes the following\n\norder:\n\nCitation\n\n1. This order may be cited as the Printing Presses and Publications\n\n(Control of Undesirable Publications) (No. 4) Order 2023.\n\nProhibition\n\n2. The printing, importation, production, reproduction, publishing, sale, issue,\n\ncirculation, distribution or possession of the publication described in the Schedule\n\nwhich is likely to be prejudicial to morality is absolutely prohibited throughout Malaysia.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n(1)\n\nTitle of\n\nPublication\n\n(2)\n\nAuthor\n\n(3)\n\nPublisher\n\n(4)\n\nLanguage\n\nWhen I Was A Kid 3 Cheeming Boey Grey Pigeon\n\nSdn. Bhd.\n\nEnglish\n\nMade 15 September 2023\n\n[KDN.PKK.S.600-16/15/123; PN(PU2)417/Jld. 26]\n\nDATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\n Minister of Home Affairs"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3766"] = {"id":"MY-H3766","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2024&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2024年大学与大学学院（马来西亚博特拉大学章程）（修正）令","en":"UNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES (CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI PUTRA MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2024","orig":"UNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES (CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI PUTRA MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2024","ms":"Perintah Universiti dan Kolej Universiti (Perlembagaan Universiti Putra Malaysia) (Pindaan) 2024","vi":"Lệnh về Các trường đại học và cao đẳng đại học (Hiến chương Đại học Putra Malaysia) (Sửa đổi) năm 2024","th":"คำสั่งมหาวิทยาลัยและวิทยาลัยมหาวิทยาลัย (ข้อบังคับมหาวิทยาลัยปุตรามาเลเซีย) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2024","id":"Perintah Universitas dan Kolese Universitas (Anggaran Dasar Universitas Putra Malaysia) (Perubahan) Tahun 2024"},"level":"regulation","category":"01_宪法与基础法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2024","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\01_宪法与基础法\\2024_P.U.(A)283-2024_UNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES (CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI PUTRA MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3766-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Universiti dan Kolej Universiti\n(Perlembagaan Universiti Putra Malaysia) (Pindaan) 2024.\n\n           (2)    Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 2 Oktober 2024.\n\nPindaan seksyen 57"}},{"id":"MY-H3766-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perlembagaan Universiti Putra Malaysia [P.U. (A) 448/2010] dipinda\ndalam seksyen 57—\n\n(a) dalam subseksyen (5), dengan menggantikan perkataan \"satu tahun\"\ndengan perkataan \"satu tahun akademik\";\n\n(b) dengan memasukkan selepas subseksyen (5) subseksyen yang berikut:\n\n\"(5A) Walau apa pun subseksyen (5), Lembaga boleh\nmengurangkan atau melanjutkan tempoh ke anggotaan MPP dan\npemegang jawatannya.\";\n\n(c) dengan memotong subseksyen (11);\n\n(d) dengan memasukkan selepas subseksyen (11) sebagaimana yang dipotong\nsubseksyen yang berikut:\n\n     \"(11A)  Universiti boleh menubuhkan apa-apa kumpulan wang atau\nmemiliki apa -apa harta untuk diuruskan atau disenggara  oleh MPP\nmengikut tatacara kewangan Universiti.\n\n (11B)  Walau apa pun subseksyen (11 A), MPP boleh, tertakluk\nkepada mana -mana undang -undang bertulis, menubuhkan,\nmenguruskan atau menyenggara apa -apa kumpulan wang mengikut\ncara sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam peraturan -peraturan yang\ndibuat oleh Lembaga.\"; dan\n\n(e) dengan memasukkan selepas subseksyen (12) subseksyen yang berikut:\n\n\"(12A)  Bagi maksud seksyen 15 A Akta, Lembaga boleh membuat\nperaturan-peraturan untuk menetapkan cara bagi pembuatan atau\npenganjuran, atau pengambilan bahagian dalam , pungutan wang atau\npenerimaan wang atau sumbangan lain oleh MPP.\".\n\nDibuat 1 Oktober 2024\n[KPT.PUU(S).100-1/21/1(11); PN(PU2)75C/V]\n\n                     Dengan Titah Perintah\n\n     DATO' SERI DIRAJA DR. ZAMBRY BIN ABD KADIR\n   Menteri Pendidikan Tinggi\n\n   UNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES ACT 1971\n\nUNIVERSITIES AND UNIVERSITY COLLEGES\n(CONSTITUTION OF THE UNIVERSITI PUTRA MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT)\nORDER 2024\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 8(3) of the Universities and\nUniversity Colleges Act 1971  [Akta 30 ], the Yang di -Pertuan Agong makes\nthe following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3767"] = {"id":"MY-H3767","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2025&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2025年联邦道路（私营管理）（通行费征收）（吉隆坡—加叻大道）（修正）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KUALA LUMPUR-KARAK HIGHWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KUALA LUMPUR-KARAK HIGHWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Pengurusan Swasta) (Kutipan Tol) (Lebuh Raya Kuala Lumpur-Karak) (Pindaan) 2025","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Quản lý tư nhân) (Thu phí đường bộ) (Đường cao tốc Kuala Lumpur-Karak) (Sửa đổi) năm 2025","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (การบริหารจัดการเอกชน) (การจัดเก็บค่าผ่านทาง) (ทางหลวงกัวลาลัมเปอร์-การัก) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2025","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Pengelolaan Swasta) (Pemungutan Tol) (Jalan Raya Kuala Lumpur-Karak) (Perubahan) Tahun 2025"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2025","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2025_P.U.(A)283-2025_FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KUALA LUMPUR-KARAK HIGHWAY) (AMENDMEN.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3767-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan\n\n(Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol) (Lebuhraya Kuala Lumpur-Karak)\n\n(Pindaan) 2025.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 31 Ogos 2025.\n\nPindaan Jadual Ketiga"}},{"id":"MY-H3767-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan (Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol)\n\n(Lebuhraya Kuala Lumpur-Karak) 1994 [P.U. (A) 369/1994] dipinda dalam Jadual Ketiga\n\ndengan memasukkan selepas butiran 8 butiran yang berikut:\n\n\"9. Mana-mana kenderaan Kerajaan yang mempunyai lambang rasmi\n\nJabatan Pengangkutan Jalan yang dilekatkan pada bahagian kiri dan kanan\n\nbadan kenderaan itu, dan dilekatkan secara kekal dengan lampu amaran\n\nkhas yang memancarkan cahaya berkelip biru pada bumbung kenderaan\n\nitu, bagi maksud menjalankan tugas penguatkuasaan.\".\n\nDibuat 26 Ogos 2025\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/43; PN(PU2)426/JLD.73]\n\nDATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\nMenteri Kerja Raya\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) ACT 1984\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS)\n\n(KUALA LUMPUR-KARAK HIGHWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2025\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of the Federal Roads\n\n(Private Management) Act 1984 [Act 306], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-8"};
  FT["MY-H3768"] = {"id":"MY-H3768","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 283/2026&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2026年联邦道路（私营管理）（通行费征收）（吉隆坡—瓜拉雪兰莪大道）（修正）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KL-KUALA SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2026","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KL-KUALA SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2026","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Pengurusan Swasta) (Kutipan Tol) (Lebuh Raya KL-Kuala Selangor) (Pindaan) 2026","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Quản lý tư nhân) (Thu phí đường bộ) (Đường cao tốc KL-Kuala Selangor) (Sửa đổi) năm 2026","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (การบริหารจัดการเอกชน) (การจัดเก็บค่าผ่านทาง) (ทางด่วน KL-กัวลอาเซอลาโงร์) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2026","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Pengelolaan Swasta) (Pemungutan Tol) (Jalan Tol KL-Kuala Selangor) (Perubahan) Tahun 2026"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA283","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 5 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2026_P.U.(A)283-2026_FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KL-KUALA SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDM.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H3768-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan tiga atau\n\nempat roda (tidak termasuk teksi dan bas)\n\n2.50"}},{"id":"MY-H3768-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan lima atau\n\nenam roda (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n5.00"}},{"id":"MY-H3768-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar atau lebih (tidak\n\ntermasuk bas)\n\n7.50"}},{"id":"MY-H3768-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Teksi 1.30"}},{"id":"MY-H3768-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Bas 2.00\n\nBagi maksud mengira bilangan gandar dan roda sesebuah kenderaan, gandar dan roda\n\nmana-mana treler yang ditarik oleh kenderaan itu hendaklah dikira sebagai sebahagian\n\ndaripada gandar dan roda kenderaan itu.\n\nBAHAGIAN II\n\nKADAR TOL BAGI PLAZA TOL KUNDANG TIMUR DAN PLAZA TOL KUNDANG BARAT\n\nDARI 1 JANUARI 2015 HINGGA 28 OKTOBER 2048\n\n(1)\n\nKelas kenderaan\n\n(2)\n\nTol kena dibayar\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan tiga atau\n\nempat roda (tidak termasuk teksi dan bas)\n\n1.30\n\n2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan lima atau\n\nenam roda (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n2.60\n\n3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar atau lebih (tidak\n\ntermasuk bas)\n\n3.90\n\n4. Teksi 0.70\n\n5. Bas 1.30\n\nBagi maksud mengira bilangan gandar dan roda sesebuah kenderaan, gandar dan roda\n\nmana-mana treler yang ditarik oleh kenderaan itu hendaklah dikira sebagai sebahagian\n\ndaripada gandar dan roda kenderaan itu.\n\nBAHAGIAN III\n\nKADAR TOL BAGI PLAZA TOL ECO GRANDEUR\n\nDARI 7 OGOS 2026 HINGGA 28 OKTOBER 2048\n\n(1)\n\nKelas kenderaan\n\n(2)\n\nTol kena dibayar\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan tiga atau\n\nempat roda (tidak termasuk teksi dan bas)\n\n1.15\n\n2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan lima atau\n\nenam roda (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n2.30\n\n3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar atau lebih (tidak\n\ntermasuk bas)\n\n3.45\n\n4. Teksi 0.57\n\n5. Bas 1.15\n\nBagi maksud mengira bilangan gandar dan roda sesebuah kenderaan, gandar dan roda\n\nmana-mana treler yang ditarik oleh kenderaan itu hendaklah dikira sebagai sebahagian\n\ndaripada gandar dan roda kenderaan itu.\".\n\nPindaan Jadual Kedua\n\n5. Perintah ibu dipinda dalam Jadual Kedua dengan memasukkan selepas PETA\n\nLEBUH RAYA KL-KUALA SELANGOR peta yang berikut:\n\n\"PETA PERSIMPANGAN BERTINGKAT ECO GRANDEUR\n\nDibuat 5 Ogos 2026\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/39; PN(PU2)426/JLD.75]\n\nDATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\nMenteri Kerja Raya\n\n\".\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) ACT 1984\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS)\n\n(KL-KUALA SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2026\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of the Federal Roads\n\n(Private Management) Act 1984 [Act 306], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) This order may be cited as the Federal Roads (Private Management)\n\n(Collection of Tolls) (KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway) (Amendment) Order 2026.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 7 August 2026.\n\nAmendment of paragraph 2\n\n2. The Federal Roads (Private Management) (Collection of Tolls) (KL-Kuala Selangor\n\nExpressway) Order 2014 [P.U. (A) 344/2014], which is referred to as the \"principal Order\"\n\nin this Order, is amended by substituting for paragraph 2 the following paragraph:\n\n\"Authorization to collect tolls\n\n 2. (1) The KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway Berhad is authorized—\n\n(a) for the period from 1 January 2015 to 28 October 2048 to\n\ndemand, collect and retain the appropriate tolls specified in\n\ncolumn (2) of the First Schedule for the use in either direction\n\nof any part of the road known as the\n\nKL-Kuala Selangor Expressway commencing from kilometre\n\n0.00 at coordinates N 366573.829, E 375376.712 of the\n\nRectified Skew Orthomorphic (RSO) Geocentric Datum of\n\nMalaysia (GDM2000) Grid and ending at kilometre 30.70\n\nat coordinates N 364885.563, E 401792.132 of the Rectified\n\nSkew Orthomorphic (RSO) Geocentric Datum of Malaysia\n\n(GDM2000) Grid, including the Ijok Interchange, Ijok Toll\n\nPlaza, Puncak Alam Interchange, Kuang Barat Toll Plaza,\n\nKundang Timur Toll Plaza, Kundang Interchange, Kundang\n\nBarat Toll Plaza, Kuang Timur Toll Plaza, Kuang Interchange,\n\nTaman Rimba Templer Toll Plaza, Taman Rimba Templer\n\nInterchange and its link roads, being a distance of 30.70\n\nkilometres, by the classes of vehicles specified in column (1)\n\nof the First Schedule; and\n\n(b) for the period from 7 August 2026 to 28 October 2048 to\n\ndemand, collect and retain the appropriate tolls specified in\n\ncolumn (2) of the First Schedule for the use in either\n\ndirection of any part of the road known as the\n\nKL-Kuala Selangor Expressway commencing from kilometre\n\n6.69 at coordinates N 363909.494, E 380581.273 of the\n\nRectified Skew Orthomorphic (RSO) Geocentric Datum of\n\nMalaysia (GDM2000) Grid and ending at kilometre 7.77 at\n\ncoordinates N 363982.727, E 381658.419 of the Rectified\n\nSkew Orthomorphic (RSO) Geocentric Datum of Malaysia\n\n(GDM2000) Grid, both distances are measured from\n\nkilometer 0.00 of the KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway at the\n\nIjok Interchange including the Eco Grandeur Toll Plaza and\n\nits link roads and ending at the Limit of Maintenance\n\nResponsibility (LMR) at coordinates N 363016.702,\n\nE 380991.224 of the Rectified Skew Orthomorphic (RSO)\n\nGeocentric Datum of Malaysia (GDM2000) Grid, by\n\nthe classes of vehicles specified in column (1) of\n\nthe First Schedule.\n\n(2) The roads specified in subparagraph (1) for the use of which\n\ntolls are authorized to be demanded, collected and retained are shown on\n\nthe maps in the Second Schedule.\".\n\nAmendment of paragraph 3\n\n3. The principle Order is amended in subparagraph 3(1) by substituting for the\n\nwords \"and Taman Rimba Templer Toll Plaza situated at kilometre 25.75 at coordinates\n\nN 363934.443, E 398646.808 RSO Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid\" the words\n\n\", Taman Rimba Templer Toll Plaza situated at kilometre 26.75 at coordinates\n\nN 363934.443, E 398646.808 RSO Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid and Eco Grandeur\n\nToll Plaza situated at N 363248.289, E 381155.308 RSO Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid\".\n\nSubstitution of First Schedule\n\n4. The principal Order is amended by substituting for the First Schedule the\n\nfollowing schedule:\n\n\"FIRST SCHEDULE\n\n[Subparagraph 2(1)]\n\nPART I\n\nRATES OF TOLLS FOR IJOK TOLL PLAZA, KUANG BARAT TOLL PLAZA, KUANG TIMUR\n\nTOLL PLAZA AND TAMAN RIMBA TEMPLER TOLL PLAZA\n\nFROM 1 JANUARY 2015 TO 28 OCTOBER 2048\n\n(1)\n\nClasses of vehicles\n\n(2)\n\nToll payable\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three or four wheels\n\n(excluding taxis and buses)\n\n2.50\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or six wheels\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n5.00\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more (excluding buses) 7.50\n\n4. Taxis 1.30\n\n5. Buses 2.00\n\nFor the purpose of calculating the number of axles and wheels of a vehicle, the axles and\n\nwheels of any trailer towed by the vehicle shall be calculated as part of the axles and\n\nwheels of the vehicles.\n\nPART II\n\nRATES OF TOLLS FOR KUNDANG TIMUR TOLL PLAZA AND KUNDANG BARAT\n\nTOLL PLAZA\n\nFROM 1 JANUARY 2015 TO 28 OCTOBER 2048\n\n(1)\n\nClasses of vehicles\n\n(2)\n\nToll payable\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three or four wheels\n\n(excluding taxis and buses)\n\n1.30\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or six wheels\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n2.60\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more (excluding buses) 3.90\n\n4. Taxis 0.70\n\n5. Buses 1.30\n\nFor the purpose of calculating the number of axles and wheels of a vehicle, the axles and\n\nwheels of any trailer towed by the vehicle shall be calculated as part of the axles and\n\nwheels of the vehicles.\n\nPART III\n\nRATES OF TOLLS FOR ECO GRANDEUR TOLL PLAZA\n\nFROM 7 AUGUST 2026 TO 28 OCTOBER 2048\n\n(1)\n\nClasses of vehicles\n\n(2)\n\nToll payable\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three or four wheels\n\n(excluding taxis and buses)\n\n1.15\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or six wheels\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n2.30\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more (excluding buses) 3.45\n\n4. Taxis 0.57\n\n5. Buses 1.15\n\nFor the purpose of calculating the number of axles and wheels of a vehicle, the axles and\n\nwheels of any trailer towed by the vehicle shall be calculated as part of the axles and\n\nwheels of the vehicles.\".\n\nAmendment of Second Schedule\n\n5. The principal Order is amended in the Second Schedule by inserting after the\n\nMAP OF KL-KUALA SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY the following map:\n\n\"MAP OF ECO GRANDEUR INTERCHANGE\n\nMade 5 August 2026\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/39; PN(PU2)426/JLD.75]\n\nDATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\nMinister of Works\n\n\"."}}],"pack":"my-8"};
